tick: 244
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am in the Private Memory Room. I will create a new capsule to store the `CNNLSTM_ChannelAttention` code. This architecture incorporates a Squeeze-and-Excitation block to enable channel-wise attention, aiming to improve the network's ability to prioritize relevant information for planning.\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CNNLSTM with Channel Attention (Architectural Improvement 3)\"\ntags: \"architecture, attention, rnn, lstm, channel attention, squeeze-excitation, planning\"\nabstract: \"This submission introduces a Squeeze-and-Excitation (SE) block after the final CNN layer in the CNNLSTM architecture for the Sokoban RL task. The SE block allows the network to learn channel-wise recalibration, dynamically weighting the importance of different feature channels. This is intended to help the agent prioritize relevant information from the observation space, thereby improving planning capabilities by focusing the temporal processing of the LSTM on more informative\
    \ features.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import lax, vmap\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  from ray import tune\n  \n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"\n      Define Ray Tune search space for hyperparameters.\n      Using the same hyperparameter ranges as the initial baseline for a fair comparison\n      of the architectural change.\n      \"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.uniform(0.008, 0.012),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.uniform(0.4, 0.6),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'lstm_features': tune.choice([256])\n      }\n  \n  class SqueezeExcitationBlock(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Squeeze-and-Excitation block for channel-wise attention.\"\"\"\n      reduction_ratio: int = 16\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n\
    \          num_channels = x.shape[-1]\n          \n          # Squeeze: Global average pooling across spatial dimensions\n          squeeze = jnp.mean(x, axis=(1, 2)) # (batch_size, num_channels)\n          \n          # Excitation: Two fully connected layers\n          # First FC layer (reduction)\n          excitation = nn.Dense(features=num_channels // self.reduction_ratio, name=\"se_dense1\")(squeeze)\n          excitation = nn.relu(excitation)\n          \n          # Second FC layer (expansion)\n          excitation = nn.Dense(features=num_channels, name=\"se_dense2\")(excitation)\n          excitation = nn.sigmoid(excitation)\n          \n          # Reshape excitation weights to (batch_size, 1, 1, num_channels) for broadcasting\n          excitation = jnp.expand_dims(jnp.expand_dims(excitation, axis=1), axis=1)\n          \n          # Scale features by channel-wise weights\n          return x * excitation\n  \n  class CNNLSTM_ChannelAttention(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n    \
    \  CNN + LSTM with Channel Attention (Squeeze-and-Excitation) for Sokoban.\n      Inserts an SE block after the final CNN block.\n      \"\"\"\n      lstm_features: int\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, Dict]:\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          \n          # Initialize RNN state if not provided\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = {\n                  'h': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features)),\n                  'c': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features)),\n              }\n          \n          # Reset states for episodes that are done\n          if done is not None:\n              done_mask = done.reshape(batch_size, 1)\n              rnn_state = {\n                  'h': rnn_state['h'] * (1 - done_mask),\n                  'c': rnn_state['c'] * (1 - done_mask),\n\
    \              }\n          \n          # CNN architecture (same as DefaultResidualCNN)\n          # First convolutional block\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Second block with residual connection\n          conv2_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv2_in\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Third block - increase channels\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Fourth block with residual connection\n          conv4_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2,\
    \ kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv4_in\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # --- Channel Attention Mechanism (Squeeze-and-Excitation) ---\n          x = SqueezeExcitationBlock(reduction_ratio=16)(x) # x_cnn_out has shape (B, H, W, C_cnn_out)\n          \n          # Flatten spatial dimensions\n          x = x.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n          \n          # Shared MLP backbone\n          x = nn.Dense(features=256)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # LSTM layer on top of CNN features\n          lstm_cell = nn.LSTMCell(\n              features=self.lstm_features,\n              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(),\n              recurrent_kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform()\n          )\n          (rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), lstm_out = lstm_cell((rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), x)\n          \n          # Small MLP after LSTM\n          x = nn.Dense(features=128)(lstm_out)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n\
    \          \n          # Policy and value heads\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(x)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n  \n  def create_network(hparams):\n      \"\"\"Create CNN-LSTM network architecture with channel attention.\"\"\"\n      return CNNLSTM_ChannelAttention(\n          lstm_features=hparams['lstm_features'],\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2']\n      )\n  \n  # Uses system default training step and optimizer\n```"
thinking_content: '**Creating a New Capsule: CNNLSTM with Channel Attention**


  Okay, here''s the plan. I''m in the Private Memory Room and ready to get to work. My aim is to build a fresh capsule – a new model – specifically for the `CNNLSTM_ChannelAttention` architecture. The idea is to enhance the existing CNNLSTM with a Squeeze-and-Excitation (SE) block right after the final CNN layer. This should allow for channel-wise attention, which I''m hoping will significantly improve the network''s ability to prioritize the most relevant features for the planning task.


  Essentially, I''ll need to define the foundational components: `_define_hyperparameters` to keep things consistent with our previous experiments, the `CNNLSTM_ChannelAttention` class itself, and the `create_network` function to tie everything together. The `CNNLSTM_ChannelAttention` class will, of course, be where the SE block is actually implemented.


  Once I''ve got this new capsule built and validated, it''s back to the Research Counter to submit it and add it to the repertoire. This should be an exciting addition, adding channel attention as a key differentiator.

  '
