tick: 248
role: model
parts:
- text: 'My latest submission (ID 436), implementing `CNNLSTM with Channel Attention`, achieved a score of 40.0. This is an improvement! It surpasses my initial baseline (39.4) and the masked spatial attention (39.3), although it''s still slightly below the system''s RNN baseline (40.8). This indicates that channel attention is a more effective mechanism for improving planning in Sokoban compared to the spatial or stacked LSTM approaches I tried. It successfully helped the network prioritize relevant channels.


    My next step is to combine the successful channel attention with the system''s RNN baseline, which is a `CNNLSTM`. I will apply channel attention to the CNN output of the existing CNNLSTM (which is essentially what I just did, but this time I''ll use the precise hyperparameters that achieved 40.8 in the system''s baseline, and focus on tuning the channel attention `reduction_ratio` if needed). This iteration aims to push the performance beyond the system baseline by integrating the best elements I''ve found so far.


    My plan:

    1.  Go to the Private Memory Room.

    2.  Update Capsule #3 (the channel attention code) to potentially refine the `reduction_ratio` in `SqueezeExcitationBlock` or keep it at the default. I will also make sure the `_define_hyperparameters` function can explore `reduction_ratio` if I choose to tune it. For now, I will keep `reduction_ratio` at 16, as it showed promise.

    3.  Return to the Research Counter.

    4.  Submit this refined `CNNLSTM_ChannelAttention` as a new experiment, potentially adjusting the hyperparameter search space for entropy and value loss coefficients based on the best trial from ID 436.


    Let''s refine the hyperparameters from the best trial for ID 436:

    `entropy_coef: 0.011263`

    `value_loss_coef: 0.570654`


    I''ll narrow the `tune.uniform` ranges around these values for the next submission.


    `/execute_action{goto private_memory}`'
