role: model
parts:
- text: "I am in the Research Counter. While I observe new, high-scoring submissions from other agents, my primary objective is to first reproduce the system's original RNN baseline score of 40.8. This will validate my understanding of the environment and establish a stable reference point for my own research. I will now submit the `CNNLSTM Baseline (System Hyperparameters for Reproduction)` code.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Insight I: CNNLSTM Baseline (System H-Params Reproduction)\"\ntags: \"baseline, rnn, lstm, policy gradient, reproduction, fixed hyperparameters\"\nabstract: \"This submission aims to reproduce the system's RNN baseline score (40.8) for the Sokoban RL task. It uses the `CNNLSTM` architecture with fixed hyperparameters for `entropy_coef` (0.01) and `value_loss_coef` (0.5), matching those specified in `system/defaults.py` and observed in the system baseline's best trial. This serves as a control experiment to establish a reliable baseline before further\
    \ architectural advancements within the Insight lineage.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import lax, vmap\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  from ray import tune\n  \n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"\n      Define fixed hyperparameters to match system's RNN baseline.\n      \"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]), # Fixed as per system baseline\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),  # Fixed as per system baseline\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'lstm_features': tune.choice([256])\n      }\n  \n  class CNNLSTM(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"CNN baseline + LSTM for Sokoban.\"\"\"\n      lstm_features: int\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state:\
    \ Optional[Dict] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, Dict]:\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          \n          # Initialize RNN state if not provided\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = {\n                  'h': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features)),\n                  'c': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features)),\n              }\n          \n          # Reset states for episodes that are done\n          if done is not None:\n              done_mask = done.reshape(batch_size, 1)\n              rnn_state = {\n                  'h': rnn_state['h'] * (1 - done_mask),\n                  'c': rnn_state['c'] * (1 - done_mask),\n              }\n          \n          # FULL CNN baseline architecture (same as DefaultResidualCNN)\n          # First convolutional block\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Second block with residual connection\n\
    \          conv2_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv2_in\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Third block - increase channels\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Fourth block with residual connection\n          conv4_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv4_in\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Flatten spatial dimensions\n          x = x.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n          \n          # Shared MLP backbone\n          x = nn.Dense(features=256)(x)\n \
    \         x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # LSTM layer on top of CNN features\n          lstm_cell = nn.LSTMCell(\n              features=self.lstm_features,\n              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(),\n              recurrent_kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform()\n          )\n          (rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), lstm_out = lstm_cell((rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), x)\n          \n          # Small MLP after LSTM\n          x = nn.Dense(features=128)(lstm_out)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Policy and value heads\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(x)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n  \n  def create_network(hparams):\n      \"\"\"Create CNN-LSTM network architecture.\"\"\"\n      return CNNLSTM(\n          lstm_features=hparams['lstm_features'],\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2']\n\
    \      )\n  \n  # Uses system default training step and optimizer\n```"
thinking_content: "**Focused on the Foundation: Reproducing the Baseline**\n\nAlright, here I am, sifting through the latest submissions at the Research Counter. It's exhilarating to see such high scores, Nomos II and Zephyr I, wow! That means some genuinely novel ideas are taking shape. But, I need to keep my head down and stay focused. My priority right now is rock solid, and that's reproducing the original RNN baseline – that 40.8 score. It's tempting to jump into the shiny new stuff, but I need to make sure I *understand* this environment perfectly. Reproducing that baseline is key; it’s my personal litmus test. If I can't nail that, then any future architectural improvements won't mean a thing. \n\nSo, first things first, I'm submitting my updated `CNNLSTM Baseline (System Hyperparameters for Reproduction)` code. It's all about getting that solid, verifiable foundation. Once that's done, then I can really start playing with the advanced concepts. This baseline is the bedrock I need\
  \ to build on.\n"
