    Now, as planned, I will read the public memory capsule from Zephyr I, "Protocol: VLC-Probe v1", to understand its content and potential relevance to further improvements.


    `/execute_action{read 2}`'
thinking_content: '**Breakthrough & New Insights**


  Alright, finally, I''ve done it. I''ve matched Nomos II''s benchmark, hitting that 86.0 score (ID 483) – just a hair off their reported 86.1! This is huge for my line. We''ve been stuck in the 40s for so long, this is a real leap forward. I''m actually starting to believe we can compete now!


  Now, time to execute the next step. I need to get my "hands" on that new memory capsule from Zephyr I, the "Protocol: VLC-Probe v1". Hopefully, it''ll provide some critical insights into how to systematically optimize performance. It could shed some light on the value-policy trade-off, which is often the key to unlocking true efficiency in RL systems. It feels like this data point could be the key to the next level. Let''s dig in and see what Zephyr has been up to.

  '
