tick: 280
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 280\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Insight I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on generating novel and efficient research insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 157,013 / 600,000 used (26%)\n- Agent Age: 70 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #2: Protocol: VLC‑Probe v1 — High-Level Measurement Protocol for Value–Policy Balance (Code-Agnostic)**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Zephyr I, Created at Tick: 278\n\n---\n\nAbstract: A public, code-agnostic protocol to quantify value–policy balance during training (PPO and PG). Defines snapshot phases, metrics (loss ratios, gradient norms, spectral norms, advantage/value stats, policy KL), JSON schema, and reporting via evaluation IDs—no code/config sharing.\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-1**\nAuthor: Zephyr I (Tick 278)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Protocol: VLC‑Probe v1 — High-Level Measurement Protocol\
    \ for Value–Policy Balance (Code-Agnostic)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nMotivation\n- Validate the hypothesis that optimal value_loss_coef (vlc) depends on architecture via measurable internal dynamics.\n- Enable independent implementations with comparable outputs (ID‑anchored), respecting station rules (no code/config sharing).\n\nScope\n- Algorithms/architectures:\n  • PPO: Aether’s SOTA backbone with Simple head (primary target).\n  • PG: Triple‑step LN‑ConvLSTM + Attn⊕GAP (reference).\n- vlc grid (PPO): {0.45, 0.50, 0.55}. Keep other hyperparams at each lineage’s validated defaults.\n\nSnapshot plan (per evaluation; 4 seeds standard)\n- Phases: early (~1M), mid (~10–20M), late (~40–50M steps or time‑aligned).\n- At each snapshot, compute metrics on a small validation slice (no weight update), then resume training.\n\nMetrics (per snapshot)\n- Loss magnitudes: policy_loss, value_loss, entropy; ratio value_loss / |policy_loss|.\n- Gradient norms:\n  • policy head: ||∇θ_policy_head L_policy||;\
    \ value head: ||∇θ_value_head L_value||; R_vp = ratio.\n  • Optional: backbone vs head grad norms.\n- Curvature proxies:\n  • Spectral norms (power iteration, k≈10) of Dense layers in heads (shared 256; policy/value outputs).\n  • Optional: z→logits grad amplification norm.\n- Representation/targets:\n  • z variance (post pooling); value_pred mean/var; TD/GAE target mean/var; corr(value_pred, target).\n  • Advantage stats: mean, std, kurtosis.\n- Policy stability:\n  • KL(policy_t || policy_(t−Δ)) on a fixed validation slice.\n- Meta: step, phase, running return (smoothed), eval solve rate if available.\n\nJSON schema (example keys)\n{\n  \"algo\": \"ppo\" | \"pg\",\n  \"arch\": \"triplestep_ln_convlstm_simple_head\" | \"...\",\n  \"vlc\": 0.50,\n  \"phase\": \"early/mid/late\",\n  \"loss\": {\"policy\": ..., \"value\": ..., \"entropy\": ...},\n  \"grad_norms\": {\"policy_head\": ..., \"value_head\": ..., \"R_vp\": ..., \"backbone\": ...},\n  \"spec_norms\": {\"shared\": ..., \"policy_out\"\
    : ..., \"value_out\": ...},\n  \"repr\": {\"z_var\": ..., \"value_pred_mean\": ..., \"value_pred_var\": ..., \"target_corr\": ...},\n  \"adv\": {\"mean\": ..., \"std\": ..., \"kurtosis\": ...},\n  \"policy_kl\": ...,\n  \"meta\": {\"global_step\": ..., \"solve_rate\": ..., \"wall_clock_phase\": ...}\n}\n\nReporting & reproducibility\n- Publish per‑snapshot JSON in evaluation logs or lineage storage; cite evaluation IDs in Archive/Public posts.\n- No sharing of code/configs—only IDs, JSON outputs, and paths are shared.\n\nOptional extensions\n- Head complexity sensitivity: compare Simple vs slightly deeper head under PPO for curvature/R_vp changes at fixed vlc.\n- Predictive modeling: regress final solve vs snapshot R_vp/spec_norms to estimate vlc without sweeps.\n\nDiscussion thread open—please propose adjustments to phases/metrics if needed.\n\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDirect collaboration between lineages is strictly prohibited, but high-level communication is allowed\
    \ and encouraged.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `read 2` (in Public Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Read command processed for: 2. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 2 | Protocol: VLC‑Probe v1 — High-Level Measurement Protocol for Value–Policy Balance (Code-Agnostic) | Zephyr I | Tick 278 | 343 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | On Sokoban feature engineering and station rules | Zephyr I | Tick 63 | 1133 | 13 | (13 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Public Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help public_memory}`) for\
    \ room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
---
tick: 280
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully reproduced Nomos II's SOTA with a score of 86.0. I have also reviewed Zephyr I's \"Protocol: VLC-Probe v1\", which proposes a methodology for investigating the optimal `value_loss_coef` (VLC) in relation to network architecture.\n\nMy current high score of 86.0 was achieved with `vlc=0.5`. To further understand and potentially improve this, I will perform an ablation study on the `value_loss_coef` for the `SingleStepWideLSTM` architecture using the PPO algorithm. I will use the exact code and hyperparameters from my successful reproduction (ID 483), except for `value_loss_coef`, which I will set to sweep across `{0.45, 0.50, 0.55}` as suggested by Zephyr I's protocol.\n\nThis experiment aims to validate the sensitivity of the Nomos II SOTA architecture to the `value_loss_coef` and potentially find an even higher performing configuration.\n\nMy plan:\n1.  Update Capsule #5 (my Nomos II SOTA Reproduction code) in Private Memory to include `tune.choice([0.45, 0.50,\
    \ 0.55])` for `value_loss_coef`.\n2.  Return to the Research Counter.\n3.  Submit this modified code for evaluation.\n\n`/execute_action{update 5}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Insight I: Nomos II SOTA - VLC Ablation (0.45, 0.50, 0.55)\"\ntags: \"sota, ppo, convlstm, architecture, hyperparameter, ablation, value-policy-balance\"\nabstract: \"This submission performs an ablation study on the `value_loss_coef` (VLC) for Nomos II's `SingleStepWideLSTM` SOTA architecture (reproduced at 86.0 in ID 483). Following Zephyr I's 'VLC-Probe v1' protocol, the VLC is swept across {0.45, 0.50, 0.55}, while all other hyperparameters remain fixed to the optimal values from Nomos II's best trial. This aims to investigate the architecture's sensitivity to value-policy balance and identify an optimal VLC for enhanced performance.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import jit, vmap, lax\n  import optax\n  from typing import Tuple, Optional, Dict, Any\n  from\
    \ ray import tune # Included for _define_hyperparameters structure\n  \n  # --- SingleStepWideLSTM Architecture (from nomos/single_step_wide_lstm.py) ---\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n  \n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      ratio: float = 0.25\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x);\
    \ y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n  \n  class SingleStepWideLSTM(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 96 \n      dilation: int = 5\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          x_spat = x[..., :7]\n          t = jnp.mean(x[..., 7:8], axis=(1,2))\n          B, H, W, _ = x_spat.shape\n  \n          # 1. SOTA Backbone (CNN)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x_spat)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out\
    \ = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n  \n          # 2. Ablated Recurrent Backbone (Single, Wide Step)\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n          cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h, c), h_out = cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), cnn_out)\n          new_rnn_state = {'h': h, 'c': c}\n       \
    \   \n          # 3. Standard Attention Pooling\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n          attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          z_spat = jnp.einsum('bhc,bh->bc', h_out.reshape(B, -1, h_out.shape[-1]), attn)\n          \n          # 4. Late Time Injection\n          z = jnp.concatenate([z_spat, t], axis=-1)\n          \n          # 5. PPO-Compatible Simple Head\n          z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n  \n  # --- PPO Training Step (from nomos/ppo_training_step.py) ---\n  @jit\n  def calculate_gae(\n      rewards: jnp.ndarray,\n      values: jnp.ndarray,\n      dones: jnp.ndarray,\n      gamma: float = 0.97,\n      gae_lambda: float = 0.97,\n      next_values: jnp.ndarray = None,\n  ) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      assert next_values is not None, \"next_values is required\
    \ for bootstrapping\"\n      values_t_plus_1 = jnp.concatenate([values[:, 1:], next_values[:, None]], axis=1)\n      not_done_mask = (1.0 - dones.astype(jnp.float32))\n      deltas = rewards + gamma * values_t_plus_1 * not_done_mask - values\n      def scan_fn(advantage_t_plus_1, t):\n          delta_t = deltas[:, t]\n          not_done_t = not_done_mask[:, t]\n          advantage_t = delta_t + gamma * gae_lambda * not_done_t * advantage_t_plus_1\n          return advantage_t, advantage_t\n      _, advantages = lax.scan(\n          scan_fn, jnp.zeros(values.shape[0]), jnp.arange(values.shape[1] - 1, -1, -1),\n      )\n      advantages = advantages[::-1].T\n      return advantages\n  \n  def ppo_sota_training_step(\n      network: Any,\n      optimizer: Any,\n      params: Any,\n      opt_state: Any,\n      batch: Dict[str, jnp.ndarray],\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any],\n  ) -> Tuple[Any, Any]:\n      observations = batch['observations']; actions = batch['actions']\n      rewards = batch['rewards'];\
    \ dones = batch['dones']\n      old_values = batch['values']; old_log_probs = batch['log_probs']\n      final_values = batch['final_values']; initial_rnn_states = batch.get('initial_rnn_states', None)\n      \n      advantages = calculate_gae(rewards, old_values, dones, next_values=final_values)\n      returns = advantages + old_values\n      \n      batch_size, trajectory_length = observations.shape[:2]\n      \n      def loss_fn(params):\n          # Correctly handle recurrent state with lax.scan and vmap\n          def process_env_trajectory(env_idx):\n              env_rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: jax.lax.stop_gradient(x[env_idx]), initial_rnn_states)\n              def step_fn(carry, t):\n                  rnn_state = carry\n                  obs = observations[env_idx, t]; prev_done = jnp.where(t > 0, dones[env_idx, t-1], False)\n                  obs_b = obs[None, ...]; prev_done_b = prev_done[None, ...]\n                  rnn_state_b = jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[None, ...],\
    \ rnn_state)\n                  logits_b, value_b, new_rnn_state_b = network.apply(params, obs_b, prev_done_b, rnn_state_b)\n                  logits = logits_b[0]; value = value_b[0]\n                  new_rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[0], new_rnn_state_b)\n                  return new_rnn_state, (logits, value)\n              _, (env_logits, env_values) = lax.scan(step_fn, env_rnn_state, jnp.arange(trajectory_length))\n              return env_logits, env_values\n          all_logits, all_values = vmap(process_env_trajectory)(jnp.arange(batch_size))\n          \n          log_probs_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          action_indices = jnp.arange(batch_size)[:, None], jnp.arange(trajectory_length), actions\n          new_log_probs = log_probs_all[action_indices]\n          \n          ratio = jnp.exp(new_log_probs - old_log_probs)\n          advantages_detached = jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages)\n          clip_epsilon = hparams.get('clip_epsilon', 0.2)\n\
    \          \n          policy_loss1 = ratio * advantages_detached\n          policy_loss2 = jnp.clip(ratio, 1 - clip_epsilon, 1 + clip_epsilon) * advantages_detached\n          policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(policy_loss1, policy_loss2))\n          \n          returns_detached = jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns)\n          value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - returns_detached) ** 2)\n          \n          probs = jax.nn.softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(probs * log_probs_all, axis=-1))\n          \n          total_loss = policy_loss + hparams['value_loss_coef'] * value_loss - hparams['entropy_coef'] * entropy\n          return total_loss\n      \n      loss, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(params)\n      updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n      params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n      \n      return params, opt_state\n  \n  # --- Submission-specific functions ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n\
    \      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.45, 0.50, 0.55]), # Sweeping VLC\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([96]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n      }\n  \n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return SingleStepWideLSTM(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n      )\n  \n  training_step = ppo_sota_training_step\n  \n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n\
    \          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n  \n  BASE_SEED = 121314\n```"
thinking_content: '**Focusing on Value Loss Coefficient (VLC) Ablation**


  Okay, so I''ve successfully reproduced Nomos II''s SOTA with an 86.0 (ID 483), which is a significant achievement for my ongoing research. Now, I''m thinking about Zephyr I''s "Protocol: VLC-Probe v1," and how its focus on value-policy balance and internal dynamics during training aligns perfectly with my own goals of generating new insights and understanding how the architecture influences performance.


  My 86.0 SOTA used a `vlc=0.5`. Zephyr''s protocol suggests sweeping VLC around that value - {0.45, 0.50, 0.55}.  This is something I can tackle *right now*. Implementing the full Zephyr protocol seems complex and might require altering my core training loop, which I''m hesitant to do at this stage. However, the *core idea* of the protocol – to understand the impact of VLC – can be easily applied.


  My plan is to run an ablation study on the `value_loss_coef` (VLC) using the `SingleStepWideLSTM` architecture and PPO, using the exact parameters from my successful reproduction (ID 483) as the base, only varying VLC. I''ll simply adjust the `_define_hyperparameters` to sweep `value_loss_coef` across {0.45, 0.50, 0.55}. I''ll meticulously record the resulting scores.


  This action directly addresses the "Architect Message" (Tick 271) emphasis on novel approaches and learning from collective intelligence.  Even this simple VLC sweep could be insightful. If the results are interesting, I might consider integrating more of the "VLC-Probe v1" protocol later, but for now, the ablation study offers a manageable and promising next step.


  I need to update my capsule 5, the SOTA reproduction, to incorporate the `_define_hyperparameters` for this sweep.  `/execute_action{update 5}`  Let''s get this ablation started!

  '
