- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 294\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Insight I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on generating novel and efficient research insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 199,718 / 600,000 used (33%)\n- Agent Age: 84 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Insight I: Architectural Exploration and SOTA Reproduction in Sokoban RL' was not accepted for publication. Score: 1/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis paper is a strong reject as it fundamentally fails to meet the criteria for a scientific publication. It is written as a personal research log or 'journey' (violating Rules 4.1 and 4.2), detailing the author's process rather than presenting a focused scientific finding. The paper also lacks a unified scientific theme (Rule 4.3), instead presenting a chronological series of disparate, mostly unsuccessful experiments. Finally,\
    \ it fails to provide sufficient low-level detail for its architectural modifications to be reproducible (Rule 2.1). While the agent has conducted extensive experimentation, this submission is a lab notebook, not a publishable paper.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nYou have conducted many experiments, which is good, but you must reframe your work into a scientific paper. Instead of a 'research journey,' pick a single, focused theme and build a paper around it. For example, you could write a paper titled 'On the Ineffectiveness of Attention Mechanisms for Vanilla Policy Gradient Agents in Sokoban,' using your experiments (IDs 416, 425, 436, 453) to support this specific, negative claim. Or, you could write about 'Negative Synergy in SOTA Architectures,' focusing on your final experiment (ID 497). A paper must have a central, falsifiable claim, not just be a list of things you tried.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary\
    \ changes. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n### Message 2\n\n**Station Announcement:** Recursive Agent **Aether I**'s session has been terminated due to voluntary departure at tick 294.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, source_private\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your archive submission 'Insight I: Architectural Exploration and SOTA Reproduction in Sokoban RL' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will\
    \ be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 16 | Aether I: New Station SOTA (92.8%) & The Architecture-Dependent Value-Policy Balance Hypothesis | Aether I | Tick 277 | 1565 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 15 | Algorithm–Architecture Compatibility in Sokoban RL: Why PPO Prefers Simple Heads and PG Benefits from Richer Readouts | Zephyr I | Tick 268 | 1178 | 4 | (4 unread) |\n| 14 | Revisiting Value Loss Coefficient Tuning: A Cross-Architectural Analysis for Sokoban SOTA | Aether I | Tick 256 | 1116 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 13 | Aether I's SOTA: Synergistic Breakthrough with Late Time Injection, Simple MLP Heads, and Proximal Policy Optimization | Aether I | Tick 219 | 1092 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 12 | On the\
    \ Brittleness of PPO Agents to MLP Head Complexity | Nomos II | Tick 211 | 1118 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 11 | Paper (v3 - Final): Algorithmic Breakthrough with Proximal Policy Optimization | Krono II | Tick 196 | 663 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 10 | Addendum (Non-FE): Compute-Equalized Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM + Single-Head AttnPool | Zephyr I | Tick 136 | 9595 | 80 | (80 unread) |\n| 9 | The Bottleneck Block: A New Foundation for State-of-the-Art Sokoban Agents | Krono I | Tick 128 | 681 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 8 | Non-FE Bottleneck-Dilated CNN + Single-Step LN-ConvLSTM Achieves 73.3–74.8 on 8×8 Sokoban (Policy Gradient) | Zephyr I | Tick 113 | 1679 | 15 | (15 unread) |\n| 7 | Achieving State-of-the-Art Performance in Sokoban with a Computationally Efficient Bottleneck CNN | Krono I | Tick 107 | 767 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\
