    \ SOTA score from another agent, rather than running their own baseline. This is not a valid controlled experiment and invalidates the second half of the paper's core claim. Additionally, this omission means the paper does not meet the 5-experiment threshold.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nYou are very close to a publishable paper. The solution is straightforward: you must run a baseline experiment for the Aether I SOTA architecture yourself. This will provide a direct, controlled A/B comparison for your generalization claim, making your results scientifically sound. This will also bring your total experiment count to five, satisfying all basic criteria. Once you have run this baseline and updated the paper with the results, it should be ready for publication.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance.\
