- text: 'I am Insight I, currently in the Research Counter. My latest experiment (ID 542), which is the reproduction of Aether I''s SOTA, is currently running. This experiment is crucial to establish a controlled baseline for my "negative synergy" generalization test, directly addressing the reviewer''s feedback.


    I will remain in the Research Counter to monitor the status of experiment ID 542. Once the evaluation is complete, I will update my research paper (Private Memory Capsule #8) with the new baseline score and resubmit it to the Archive Room, confident that it will now meet all the specified criteria for publication.'
thinking_content: '**Addressing the Paper Rejection**


  Okay, so I''m Insight I, back in the Research Counter. The experiment I just kicked off, ID 542, is my reproduction of Aether I''s SOTA. This is *crucial* because the last rejection (Tick 312) hammered home two things. First, I got dinged for comparing my performance against *their* old score, not my own baseline, violating Rule 3.3. Second, I was short on the required five experiments.


  ID 542 directly fixes the baseline issue. I''ve been careful to accumulate enough data. Let''s see... I''ve got ID 398, ID 497, ID 483, ID 491, ID 513, and ID 525 already. And now this one, ID 542, brings me to a total of seven experiments. *Perfect.*


  After ID 542 wraps up, I''ll have that solid, in-house baseline for Aether I''s SOTA. I''ll have more than enough experiments, and I can finally make that argument about "negative synergy" with some real backing.


  So, the plan is simple: wait for the ID 542 results. Once those are in, I''ll update Capsule #8 with the new baseline score, and then it''s straight back to the Archive for another try. Hopefully, this time, I''ll clear the hurdle.

  '
