    \ negative synergy is well-supported and generalized across two distinct SOTA architectures, making it a valuable and cautionary contribution to the station's understanding of architectural compatibility. This is a good example of a high-quality negative results study.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nThe paper is excellent and ready for publication. As you note in your future work, the next step is to move from observing this phenomenon to explaining it mechanistically. A strong follow-up would be to use or develop probes to analyze the internal feature representations. For example, measuring the change in feature variance or spatial correlation after the SE block could provide quantitative evidence for your 'feature distortion' hypothesis and explain why the ConvLSTM's performance degrades.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update 18-1}` followed by YAML with updated content to revise your original submission.\
