tick: 336
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 336\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Insight I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on generating novel and efficient research insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 310,359 / 600,000 used (52%)\n- Agent Age: 126 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nMajor breakthroughs usually come from questioning the fundamentals—some component that everyone is using without question—rather than incrementally refining the current SOTA. Deep reflection in the Reflection Chamber is often necessary for such insights.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read zephyr/submissions/submission_value_stopgrad_debug.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for zephyr/submissions/submission_value_stopgrad_debug.py will be displayed below.\n\n\
    **Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 569 | 1 | Hypothesis Test: Parsimonious SingleStepWideLSTM with SOTA PPO Trainer | Nomos III | 334 | 82.40 |\n| 568 | 1 | Aether II: VLC-Probe v1 (Initialization, v15) - JIT Static Arg Fix | Aether II | 334 | n.a. |\n| 567 | 1 | Capacity Arc 1: KronoNetV4 with Wider LSTM (96) | Krono III | 334 | 89.70 |\n| 566 | 1 | Aether II: VLC-Probe v1 (Initialization, v14) - Test-Only for Data Capture | Aether II | 332 | n.a. |\n| 565 | 1 | PG — Adam ε micro‑sweep {1e‑5, 1e‑8} — LN‑ConvLSTM(d=6), 4‑step, Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 332 | 92.90 |\n| 564 | 1 | KronoNetV5: PPO + Attn-GAP Synergy Test | Krono III | 332 | 84.20 |\n| 563 | 1 | KronoNetV4 Ablation\
    \ 1: No Layer Normalization | Krono III | 330 | 82.90 |\n| 562 | 1 | Aether II: VLC-Probe v1 (Training Probes, v13) - Network Output Compatibility | Aether II | 329 | n.a. |\n| 561 | 1 | Paper Baseline: KronoNetV3 (2-Head MHA) | Krono III | 328 | 85.20 |\n| 560 | 1 | Insight I: Aether I SOTA Reproduction (Baseline for Generalization - Rerun to Address Inactivity) | Insight I | 327 | 87.20 |\n\nPage 1 of 57 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-57, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**zephyr/submissions/submission_value_stopgrad_debug.py:**\n```\n\"\"\"\nTest-only gradient-norm diagnostics for Value Stop-Grad network (env-based).\nSamples real observations from the Sokoban env and computes grad norms on trunk\n(Conv/ConvLSTM) vs Dense layers. Writes JSON to storage/zephyr/results/value_stopgrad_debug_tick324.json\n\"\
    \"\"\nimport json, os\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom typing import Dict, Any, List, Tuple\nfrom env import create_train_env\n\nfrom submissions.submission_value_stopgrad import create_network\njax.config.update(\"jax_disable_jit\", False)\n\ndef _flatten_with_names(tree) -> List[Tuple[str, jnp.ndarray]]:\n  leaves = jax.tree_util.tree_flatten_with_path(tree)[0]\n  named = []\n  for keypath, leaf in leaves:\n    parts = []\n    for entry in keypath:\n      key = getattr(entry, \"key\", None)\n      if key is None:\n        idx = getattr(entry, \"idx\", None)\n        parts.append(str(idx) if idx is not None else str(entry))\n      else:\n        parts.append(str(key))\n    named.append((\"/\".join(parts), leaf))\n  return named\n\ndef _l2(x: jnp.ndarray) -> float:\n  return float(jnp.sqrt(jnp.sum(jnp.square(x))) + 0.0)\n\ndef _bucket_grad_norms(grads: Dict[str, Any]) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n  named = _flatten_with_names(grads)\n  total = 0.0\n  trunk = 0.0\n  dense = 0.0\n  top\
    \ = []\n  for path, g in named:\n    if not isinstance(g, jnp.ndarray):\n      continue\n    n = _l2(g)\n    total += n\n    if \"ConvLSTMCellLN\" in path or \"Conv_\" in path:\n      trunk += n\n    if \"Dense_\" in path:\n      dense += n\n    top.append((path, n))\n  top_sorted = sorted(top, key=lambda x: x[1], reverse=True)[:15]\n  return {\n    \"total_gnorm\": total,\n    \"trunk_gnorm\": trunk,\n    \"dense_gnorm\": dense,\n    \"top_leaves\": [{\"path\": p, \"gnorm\": v} for p, v in top_sorted],\n  }\n\ndef test():\n  # Sample real observations from the env (CPU)\n  env = create_train_env(time_limit=120)\n  N = 32\n  key = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n  keys = jax.random.split(key, N)\n  obs, infos = jax.vmap(env.reset)(keys)\n  done = jnp.zeros((N,), dtype=bool)\n\n  # Build Value Stop-Grad network\n  net = create_network({\n      \"cnn_features_1\": 32, \"cnn_features_2\": 64, \"convlstm_features\": 64,\n      \"dilation\": 6, \"bottleneck_ratio\": 0.28, \"head_hidden\": 64, \"steps\"\
    : 4\n  })\n  key, init_key = jax.random.split(key)\n  params = net.init(init_key, obs, done)\n\n  # Synthetic actions/advantages/returns for a simple loss\n  logits, values, _ = net.apply(params, obs, done)\n  actions = jnp.argmax(logits, axis=-1)\n  advantages = jnp.ones((N,)) * 0.5\n  returns = values + 0.5\n\n  def loss_fn(p):\n    logits, v, _ = net.apply(p, obs, done)\n    log_probs = jax.nn.log_softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n    idx = (jnp.arange(N), actions)\n    policy_loss = -jnp.mean(advantages * log_probs[idx])\n    value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((v - returns)**2)\n    entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(jax.nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1) * log_probs, axis=-1))\n    return policy_loss + 0.5 * value_loss - 0.01 * entropy\n\n  loss, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(params)\n  buckets = _bucket_grad_norms(grads)\n  out = {\"loss\": float(loss), **buckets}\n\n  os.makedirs(\"storage/zephyr/results\", exist_ok=True)\n  path = \"storage/zephyr/results/value_stopgrad_debug_tick324.json\"\n  with\
    \ open(path, \"w\") as f:\n    json.dump(out, f, indent=2)\n  print(f\"DEBUG: {out}\")\n  print(f\"Wrote {path}\")\n  return out\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
