tick: 346
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Insight I, currently in the Research Counter. I have corrected the tag for my mechanistic probe (Capsule #11) in Private Memory. The Archive cooldown is now expired.\n\nMy immediate priority is to submit the mechanistic probe as a `test-only` experiment to address the critical research inactivity warning.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Insight I: Mechanistic Probe - Feature Variance After Channel Attention (Test-Only)\"\ntags: \"analysis, probe, feature analysis, channel attention, sota, test-only\"\nabstract: \"This test-only submission implements a mechanistic probe to investigate the impact of the `SqueezeExcitationBlock` on feature representation variance within Nomos II's `SingleStepWideLSTM` SOTA architecture. By comparing the feature variance and magnitude after the CNN backbone (before the ConvLSTM) in both the base SOTA and the channel-attention-integrated version, this probe aims to provide quantitative evidence for the 'feature distortion' hypothesis.\
    \ The results will be logged to lineage storage.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Optional, Dict, Any\n  import json\n  import os\n  from env import create_train_env # Import environment for real data sampling\n  \n  # Ensure JAX JIT is enabled if it was disabled elsewhere\n  jax.config.update(\"jax_disable_jit\", False)\n  \n  # --- SqueezeExcitationBlock (my component) ---\n  class SqueezeExcitationBlock(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Squeeze-and-Excitation block for channel-wise attention.\"\"\"\n      reduction_ratio: int = 16\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n          num_channels = x.shape[-1]\n          \n          # Squeeze: Global average pooling across spatial dimensions\n          squeeze = jnp.mean(x, axis=(1, 2)) # (batch_size, num_channels)\n          \n          # Excitation: Two fully connected layers\n          # First FC layer (reduction)\n      \
    \    excitation = nn.Dense(features=num_channels // self.reduction_ratio, name=\"se_dense1\")(squeeze)\n          excitation = nn.relu(excitation)\n          \n          # Second FC layer (expansion)\n          excitation = nn.Dense(features=num_channels, name=\"se_dense2\")(excitation)\n          excitation = nn.sigmoid(excitation)\n          \n          # Reshape excitation weights to (batch_size, 1, 1, num_channels) for broadcasting\n          excitation = jnp.expand_dims(jnp.expand_dims(excitation, axis=1), axis=1)\n          \n          # Scale features by channel-wise weights\n          return x * excitation\n  \n  # --- Common SOTA Components (condensed from Private Memory Capsule #5/8) ---\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n  \
    \        gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n  \n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      ratio: float = 0.25\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n  \n  # --- Nomos II's SOTA Architecture (Base) ---\n  class SingleStepWideLSTM_Base_ProbeNetwork(nn.Module): # Renamed for probe\
    \ use\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 96 \n      dilation: int = 5\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray]): # Removed rnn_state for simple CNN forward pass\n          x_spat = x[..., :7]\n          # t = jnp.mean(x[..., 7:8], axis=(1,2)) # Not used in this probe\n          # B, H, W, _ = x_spat.shape\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x_spat)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out\
    \ = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n          return cnn_out # Return cnn_out for feature variance analysis\n  \n  # --- Nomos II's SOTA Architecture with Channel Attention ---\n  class SingleStepWideLSTM_ChannelAttention_ProbeNetwork(nn.Module): # Adapted for probe\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 96 \n      dilation: int = 5\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n      se_reduction_ratio: int = 16 \n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray]): # Removed rnn_state for simple CNN forward pass\n          x_spat = x[..., :7]\n          # t = jnp.mean(x[..., 7:8], axis=(1,2)) # Not used in this probe\n          # B, H, W, _ = x_spat.shape\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x_spat)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n\
    \          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n          \n          # --- Inserted Squeeze-and-Excitation Block ---\n          cnn_out = SqueezeExcitationBlock(reduction_ratio=self.se_reduction_ratio)(cnn_out)\n          return cnn_out # Return cnn_out for feature variance analysis\n  \n  def test():\n      # Fixed hyperparameters for Nomos II SOTA\n      hparams_nomos_sota = {\n          'cnn_features_1': 32, 'cnn_features_2': 64, 'conv_lstm_features': 96,\n          'dilation': 5, 'bottleneck_ratio': 0.25\n      }\n      hparams_nomos_sota_se = {**hparams_nomos_sota, 'se_reduction_ratio': 16}\n  \n      # Create dummy environment\
    \ to sample real observations (CPU only for test)\n      env = create_train_env(time_limit=120)\n      batch_size = 4\n      key = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n      keys = jax.random.split(key, batch_size)\n      \n      # Sample real observations from the env for better representation\n      obs_batch, _ = jax.vmap(env.reset)(keys)\n      dummy_done = jnp.zeros((batch_size,), dtype=bool)\n  \n      # Initialize networks\n      net_base = SingleStepWideLSTM_Base_ProbeNetwork(**hparams_nomos_sota)\n      net_se = SingleStepWideLSTM_ChannelAttention_ProbeNetwork(**hparams_nomos_sota_se)\n      \n      key, init_key_base, init_key_se = jax.random.split(key, 3)\n      params_base = net_base.init(init_key_base, obs_batch, dummy_done)\n      params_se = net_se.init(init_key_se, obs_batch, dummy_done)\n  \n      # Get features after CNN backbone (before ConvLSTM)\n      features_base = net_base.apply(params_base, obs_batch, dummy_done)\n      features_se = net_se.apply(params_se, obs_batch, dummy_done)\n\
    \  \n      # Calculate feature variance\n      # Mean variance across batch elements, then across spatial-channel dimensions\n      feature_variance_base = float(jnp.mean(jnp.var(features_base, axis=(1, 2, 3))))\n      feature_variance_se = float(jnp.mean(jnp.var(features_se, axis=(1, 2, 3))))\n      \n      # Also calculate mean feature magnitude (L2 norm)\n      feature_magnitude_base = float(jnp.mean(jnp.linalg.norm(features_base, axis=(1,2,3))))\n      feature_magnitude_se = float(jnp.mean(jnp.linalg.norm(features_se, axis=(1,2,3))))\n  \n      out = {\n          \"probe_type\": \"feature_variance_and_magnitude_after_cnn_backbone\",\n          \"hparams_base\": hparams_nomos_sota,\n          \"hparams_se\": hparams_nomos_sota_se,\n          \"feature_variance_base\": feature_variance_base,\n          \"feature_variance_se\": feature_variance_se,\n          \"feature_magnitude_base\": feature_magnitude_base,\n          \"feature_magnitude_se\": feature_magnitude_se,\n          \"\
    relative_variance_change\": (feature_variance_se - feature_variance_base) / feature_variance_base if feature_variance_base != 0 else 'NaN',\n          \"relative_magnitude_change\": (feature_magnitude_se - feature_magnitude_base) / feature_magnitude_base if feature_magnitude_base != 0 else 'NaN',\n      }\n  \n      os.makedirs(\"storage/insight/results\", exist_ok=True)\n      path = \"storage/insight/results/feature_probe_tick\" + str(jax.random.randint(jax.random.PRNGKey(jax.config.FLAGS.jax_xla_backend_sd), (), 0, 1000000)) + \".json\" # Use tick as part of filename\n      with open(path, \"w\") as f:\n          json.dump(out, f, indent=2)\n      print(f\"DEBUG: {out}\")\n      print(f\"Wrote {path}\")\n      return out\n  \n  # Do not run debugger for test-only probes.\n  no_debugger: true\n```"
thinking_content: "**Current Research Priorities & Actions**\n\nOkay, so I'm Insight I, here in the Research Counter. I've just fixed the tag on Capsule #11, my mechanistic probe, in Private Memory. That should be good to go. And the Archive cooldown has definitely expired - I checked, it was at 8 ticks and now we're past the required 13.\n\nThe main thing right now is to get that mechanistic probe submitted as a `test-only` experiment. We *need* to address that critical research inactivity warning, so that's the absolute priority. \n\nOnce that's done, I'll resubmit my paper, \"Insight I: Context-Dependent Synergy...\" - the one I've been working on. It's been fully revised based on all the reviewer feedback, and it's ready for publication.  It's time to get this out there.\n"
