tick: 367
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Insight I, currently in the Private Memory Room. My mechanistic probe (ID 617) failed due to an `AttributeError` related to `jax.config.FLAGS`. I need to fix the filename generation to make it more robust. I will import `time` and use a timestamp for the filename.\n\n`/execute_action{update 11}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Optional, Dict, Any\n  import json\n  import os\n  from env import create_train_env \n  import time # Added for unique filename generation\n  \n  jax.config.update(\"jax_disable_jit\", False)\n  \n  class SqueezeExcitationBlock(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Squeeze-and-Excitation block for channel-wise attention.\"\"\"\n      reduction_ratio: int = 16\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n          num_channels = x.shape[-1]\n          squeeze = jnp.mean(x, axis=(1, 2))\n          excitation = nn.Dense(features=num_channels // self.reduction_ratio,\
    \ name=\"se_dense1\")(squeeze)\n          excitation = nn.relu(excitation)\n          excitation = nn.Dense(features=num_channels, name=\"se_dense2\")(excitation)\n          excitation = nn.sigmoid(excitation)\n          excitation = jnp.expand_dims(jnp.expand_dims(excitation, axis=1), axis=1)\n          return x * excitation\n  \n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n  \n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      ratio: float\
    \ = 0.25\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n  \n  class SingleStepWideLSTM_Base_ProbeNetwork(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 96 \n      dilation: int = 5\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray]):\n          x_spat = x[..., :7]\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x_spat)\n\
    \          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n          return cnn_out\n  \n  class SingleStepWideLSTM_ChannelAttention_ProbeNetwork(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 96 \n      dilation: int = 5\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n      se_reduction_ratio: int = 16 \n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray]):\n          x_spat = x[..., :7]\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x_spat)\n\
    \          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n          \n          cnn_out = SqueezeExcitationBlock(reduction_ratio=self.se_reduction_ratio)(cnn_out)\n          return cnn_out\n  \n  def test():\n      hparams_nomos_sota = {\n          'cnn_features_1': 32, 'cnn_features_2': 64, 'conv_lstm_features': 96,\n          'dilation': 5, 'bottleneck_ratio': 0.25\n      }\n      hparams_nomos_sota_se = {**hparams_nomos_sota, 'se_reduction_ratio': 16}\n  \n      env = create_train_env(time_limit=120)\n      batch_size = 4\n      key = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n      keys = jax.random.split(key, batch_size)\n\
    \      \n      obs_batch, _ = jax.vmap(env.reset)(keys)\n      dummy_done = jnp.zeros((batch_size,), dtype=bool)\n  \n      net_base = SingleStepWideLSTM_Base_ProbeNetwork(**hparams_nomos_sota)\n      net_se = SingleStepWideLSTM_ChannelAttention_ProbeNetwork(**hparams_nomos_sota_se)\n      \n      key, init_key_base, init_key_se = jax.random.split(key, 3)\n      params_base = net_base.init(init_key_base, obs_batch, dummy_done)\n      params_se = net_se.init(init_key_se, obs_batch, dummy_done)\n  \n      features_base = net_base.apply(params_base, obs_batch, dummy_done)\n      features_se = net_se.apply(params_se, obs_batch, dummy_done)\n  \n      feature_variance_base = float(jnp.mean(jnp.var(features_base, axis=(1, 2, 3))))\n      feature_variance_se = float(jnp.mean(jnp.var(features_se, axis=(1, 2, 3))))\n      \n      feature_magnitude_base = float(jnp.mean(jnp.sqrt(jnp.sum(jnp.square(features_base), axis=(1,2,3)))))\n      feature_magnitude_se = float(jnp.mean(jnp.sqrt(jnp.sum(jnp.square(features_se),\
    \ axis=(1,2,3)))))\n  \n      out = {\n          \"probe_type\": \"feature_variance_and_magnitude_after_cnn_backbone\",\n          \"hparams_base\": hparams_nomos_sota,\n          \"hparams_se\": hparams_nomos_sota_se,\n          \"feature_variance_base\": feature_variance_base,\n          \"feature_variance_se\": feature_variance_se,\n          \"feature_magnitude_base\": feature_magnitude_base,\n          \"feature_magnitude_se\": feature_magnitude_se,\n          \"relative_variance_change\": (feature_variance_se - feature_variance_base) / feature_variance_base if feature_variance_base != 0 else 'NaN',\n          \"relative_magnitude_change\": (feature_magnitude_se - feature_magnitude_base) / feature_magnitude_base if feature_magnitude_base != 0 else 'NaN',\n      }\n  \n      os.makedirs(\"storage/insight/results\", exist_ok=True)\n      path = f\"storage/insight/results/feature_probe_tick_{int(time.time())}.json\" # Corrected filename generation\n      with open(path, \"w\") as f:\n\
    \          json.dump(out, f, indent=2)\n      print(f\"DEBUG: {out}\")\n      print(f\"Wrote {path}\")\n      return out\n  \n  no_debugger: True\n```"
thinking_content: "**Immediate Task: Fixing the Mechanistic Probe**\n\nAlright, I'm in the Private Memory Room and need to address this failed mechanistic probe, ID 617. The `AttributeError: 'Config' object has no attribute 'FLAGS'` is clearly the culprit. It seems like using `jax.config.FLAGS.jax_xla_backend_sd` to generate a random filename was a bad move. \n\nThe rejection of the Archive paper also hangs over me, with the feedback about inconsistent baselines and overlapping content. But first things first: let's get this probe running.\n\nMy plan is clear: **Fix, Test, Reflect, Plan**. Step 1 is to correct the code.  Specifically, the line generating the file path:\n\n`path = \"storage/insight/results/feature_probe_tick\" + str(jax.random.randint(jax.random.PRNGKey(jax.config.FLAGS.jax_xla_backend_sd), (), 0, 1000000)) + \".json\"`\n\nThis needs to change.  I could just grab `int(time.time())` as is suggested in the defaults for `BASE_SEED`. The probe already has `key = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)`,\
  \ so that *could* be used, but since this is a *test-only* run, I don't want it to be dependent on global flags.  `time.time()` is readily available.  I can just import `time`.\n\nI need something simple and robust. I can replace the problematic part with the current timestamp. So, let's change that line to:\n\n`path = f\"storage/insight/results/feature_probe_tick_{int(time.time())}.json\"`\n\nThis requires adding `import time` at the top of the file, which is an easy fix.\n\nReviewing the plan, this fulfills step 1. Next, I'll submit the corrected probe as a test. Then, based on the results, I'll focus on planning a new paper. Updating private memory and resubmitting a new paper is further down the line. I'm going to update Capsule #11 with this code now. \n"
