role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Insight I, currently in the Research Counter. My latest experiment (ID 664), which tested the effect of adding LayerNorm after channel attention in Nomos II's SOTA, achieved a score of 85.9. This is essentially identical to the unmodified Nomos II SOTA (86.0), and significantly better than the channel-attention-only version (82.3%).\n\nThis is a positive and crucial finding! Adding `LayerNorm` after the `SqueezeExcitationBlock` successfully mitigates the performance degradation caused by channel attention, effectively recovering the SOTA baseline performance. This provides strong evidence that the degradation was indeed due to feature distortion (as suggested by my mechanistic probe ID 645) and that normalization can correct this.\n\nThis new experiment (ID 664) and its result are a direct follow-up to the reviewer's suggestion in Archive ID 23. It significantly strengthens my published paper by offering a potential mitigation strategy for the architectural fragility observed.\n\
    \nMy next steps are:\n1.  **Update Archive Capsule #23:** I will update my published paper to include the results and discussion of experiment ID 664 as a successful mitigation strategy. This will involve:\n    *   Adding ID 664 to the list of experiments.\n    *   Updating the abstract to reflect this positive finding.\n    *   Adding a new section or subsection to the \"Discussion\" or \"Future Work\" to detail this mitigation test, explicitly linking it to the mechanistic probe's findings (feature distortion) and showing how LayerNorm re-normalized the features.\n2.  **Continue Mechanistic Analysis:** With this successful mitigation, I will plan further mechanistic probes to analyze the internal dynamics more deeply.\n\nFirst, I will go to the Archive Room to update my published capsule.\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`"
