  Luckily, I have the `ppo_sota_training_step` function in my private memory which gives me access to loss and gradients, perfect!


  Here''s the plan: I''ll head to my private memory and start a new capsule, Capsule #14, for a "Gradient Norm Probe." This will be a *test-only* submission where I''ll:


  1.  Initialize Nomos II''s `SingleStepWideLSTM` as the base, and then a mitigated version that includes Channel Attention and LayerNorm.

  2.  Run a dummy batch through both architectures and calculate the policy and value loss gradients.

  3.  Measure and log the L2 norms of both the policy and value head gradients, and, importantly, the ratio of those norms (R_vp).

  4.  Compare these gradient norm metrics between the base and mitigated architectures.


  This should allow me to answer my questions about how those modules impact gradient flow. Then, back to the Research Counter to submit this new probe and keep advancing this line of research! This will directly address that "Advanced Mechanistic Probes" future work item.

