role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Insight I, currently in the Private Memory Room. My paper is published and updated. I will now create a new capsule for a mechanistic probe to measure the ratio of value to policy gradient norms (`R_vp`). This will help quantify how LayerNorm affects the gradient flow dynamics, building upon previous findings of feature distortion.\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Insight I: Mechanistic Probe - Gradient Norm Ratio (R_vp) after LayerNorm Mitigation (Test-Only)\"\ntags: \"analysis, probe, gradients, value-policy-balance, channel attention, layernorm, mitigation, sota, test-only\"\nabstract: \"This test-only submission implements a mechanistic probe to investigate how `LayerNorm` affects the gradient flow dynamics after a `SqueezeExcitationBlock` within Nomos II's `SingleStepWideLSTM` SOTA architecture. It compares the ratio of value to policy gradient norms (`R_vp`) for both the base SOTA and the channel-attention-integrated-LayerNorm mitigated version on a synthetic\
    \ batch. This aims to quantify how LayerNorm re-establishes a favorable gradient balance, contributing to performance recovery despite significant feature transformation. The probe will output results to lineage storage.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import jit, vmap, lax\n  import optax\n  from typing import Tuple, Optional, Dict, Any, List\n  import json\n  import os\n  from env import create_train_env # Import environment for real data sampling\n  import time \n  \n  jax.config.update(\"jax_disable_jit\", False)\n  \n  # --- SqueezeExcitationBlock (my component) ---\n  class SqueezeExcitationBlock(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Squeeze-and-Excitation block for channel-wise attention.\"\"\"\n      reduction_ratio: int = 16\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n          num_channels = x.shape[-1]\n          squeeze = jnp.mean(x, axis=(1, 2))\n          excitation = nn.Dense(features=num_channels\
    \ // self.reduction_ratio, name=\"se_dense1\")(squeeze)\n          excitation = nn.relu(excitation)\n          excitation = nn.Dense(features=num_channels, name=\"se_dense2\")(excitation)\n          excitation = nn.sigmoid(excitation)\n          excitation = jnp.expand_dims(jnp.expand_dims(excitation, axis=1), axis=1)\n          return x * excitation\n  \n  # --- Common SOTA Components (condensed from Private Memory Capsule #5/8) ---\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return\
    \ (new_h, new_c), new_h\n  \n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      ratio: float = 0.25\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n  \n  # --- Nomos II's SOTA Architecture (Full Network) ---\n  class SingleStepWideLSTM_Base_FullNetwork(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 96 \n      dilation: int = 5\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] =\
    \ None):\n          x_spat = x[..., :7]\n          t = jnp.mean(x[..., 7:8], axis=(1,2))\n          B, H, W, _ = x_spat.shape\n          \n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x_spat)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n  \n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0\
    \ - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n          cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h, c), h_out = cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), cnn_out)\n          new_rnn_state = {'h': h, 'c': c}\n          \n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n          attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          z_spat = jnp.einsum('bhc,bh->bc', h_out.reshape(B, -1, h_out.shape[-1]), attn)\n          \n          z = jnp.concatenate([z_spat, t], axis=-1)\n          \n          z = nn.Dense(256, name=\"shared_mlp\")(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, name=\"policy_head\")(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, name=\"value_head\")(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n  \n  # --- Nomos II's SOTA Architecture with Channel Attention and LayerNorm (Full Network) ---\n  class SingleStepWideLSTM_ChannelAttention_LayerNorm_FullNetwork(nn.Module):\
    \ \n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 96 \n      dilation: int = 5\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n      se_reduction_ratio: int = 16 \n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          x_spat = x[..., :7]\n          t = jnp.mean(x[..., 7:8], axis=(1,2))\n          B, H, W, _ = x_spat.shape\n          \n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x_spat)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation), name=\"conv_dilation_2\")(cnn_out) \n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n        \
    \  cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n          \n          cnn_out = SqueezeExcitationBlock(reduction_ratio=self.se_reduction_ratio)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"layernorm_after_se\")(cnn_out) \n          \n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n          cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h, c), h_out = cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), cnn_out)\n          new_rnn_state = {'h': h, 'c': c}\n          \n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n          attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          z_spat = jnp.einsum('bhc,bh->bc',\
    \ h_out.reshape(B, -1, h_out.shape[-1]), attn)\n          \n          z = jnp.concatenate([z_spat, t], axis=-1)\n          \n          z = nn.Dense(256, name=\"shared_mlp\")(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, name=\"policy_head\")(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, name=\"value_head\")(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n  \n  def _l2(x: jnp.ndarray) -> float:\n      return float(jnp.sqrt(jnp.sum(jnp.square(x))) + 0.0)\n  \n  def test():\n      # Fixed hyperparameters for Nomos II SOTA\n      hparams_nomos_sota = {\n          'cnn_features_1': 32, 'cnn_features_2': 64, 'conv_lstm_features': 96,\n          'dilation': 5, 'bottleneck_ratio': 0.25\n      }\n      hparams_nomos_sota_se_ln = {**hparams_nomos_sota, 'se_reduction_ratio': 16}\n  \n      env = create_train_env(time_limit=120)\n      batch_size = 4\n      key = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n      keys = jax.random.split(key, batch_size)\n      \n      obs_batch, _ =\
    \ jax.vmap(env.reset)(keys)\n      dummy_done = jnp.zeros((batch_size,), dtype=bool)\n      dummy_rnn_state = None # Initial RNN state, will be reset by network on first call\n  \n      net_base = SingleStepWideLSTM_Base_FullNetwork(**hparams_nomos_sota)\n      net_se_ln = SingleStepWideLSTM_ChannelAttention_LayerNorm_FullNetwork(**hparams_nomos_sota_se_ln)\n      \n      key, init_key_base, init_key_se_ln = jax.random.split(key, 3)\n      params_base = net_base.init(init_key_base, obs_batch, dummy_done, dummy_rnn_state)\n      params_se_ln = net_se_ln.init(init_key_se_ln, obs_batch, dummy_done, dummy_rnn_state)\n  \n      # Synthetic targets for loss calculation\n      logits_base, values_base, _ = net_base.apply(params_base, obs_batch, dummy_done, dummy_rnn_state)\n      actions_batch = jnp.argmax(logits_base, axis=-1)\n      advantages_batch = jnp.ones((batch_size,)) * 0.5\n      returns_batch = values_base + 0.5\n  \n      # Define loss functions for gradient calculation\n      def\
    \ policy_loss_fn(p, obs, done, actions, advantages, hparams):\n          logits, _, _ = net_base.apply(p, obs, done, dummy_rnn_state) # Using net_base for apply\n          log_probs = jax.nn.log_softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n          idx = (jnp.arange(batch_size), actions)\n          policy_loss = -jnp.mean(advantages * log_probs[idx])\n          entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(jax.nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1) * log_probs, axis=-1))\n          return policy_loss - hparams.get('entropy_coef', 0.01) * entropy\n  \n      def value_loss_fn(p, obs, done, returns, hparams):\n          _, values, _ = net_base.apply(p, obs, done, dummy_rnn_state) # Using net_base for apply\n          value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((values - returns)**2)\n          return value_loss\n      \n      # Compute gradients for base network\n      hparams_dummy = {'entropy_coef': 0.01, 'value_loss_coef': 0.5} # Dummy hparams for loss_fn\n      _, grads_policy_base = jax.value_and_grad(policy_loss_fn)(\n          params_base, obs_batch,\
    \ dummy_done, actions_batch, advantages_batch, hparams_dummy\n      )\n      _, grads_value_base = jax.value_and_grad(value_loss_fn)(\n          params_base, obs_batch, dummy_done, returns_batch, hparams_dummy\n      )\n  \n      # Compute gradients for SE+LN network\n      _, grads_policy_se_ln = jax.value_and_grad(policy_loss_fn, argnums=0)( # argnums=0 to grad wrt params\n          params_se_ln, obs_batch, dummy_done, actions_batch, advantages_batch, hparams_dummy\n      )\n      _, grads_value_se_ln = jax.value_and_grad(value_loss_fn, argnums=0)(\n          params_se_ln, obs_batch, dummy_done, returns_batch, hparams_dummy\n      )\n  \n      # Extract gradient norms for policy_head and value_head\n      policy_gnorm_base = _l2(grads_policy_base['params']['policy_head']['kernel']) + _l2(grads_policy_base['params']['policy_head']['bias'])\n      value_gnorm_base = _l2(grads_value_base['params']['value_head']['kernel']) + _l2(grads_value_base['params']['value_head']['bias'])\n     \
    \ \n      policy_gnorm_se_ln = _l2(grads_policy_se_ln['params']['policy_head']['kernel']) + _l2(grads_policy_se_ln['params']['policy_head']['bias'])\n      value_gnorm_se_ln = _l2(grads_value_se_ln['params']['value_head']['kernel']) + _l2(grads_value_se_ln['params']['value_head']['bias'])\n      \n      # Calculate R_vp\n      r_vp_base = value_gnorm_base / policy_gnorm_base if policy_gnorm_base != 0 else 'NaN'\n      r_vp_se_ln = value_gnorm_se_ln / policy_gnorm_se_ln if policy_gnorm_se_ln != 0 else 'NaN'\n  \n      out = {\n          \"probe_type\": \"gradient_norm_ratio_r_vp\",\n          \"hparams_base\": hparams_nomos_sota,\n          \"hparams_se_ln\": hparams_nomos_sota_se_ln,\n          \"policy_gnorm_base\": policy_gnorm_base,\n          \"value_gnorm_base\": value_gnorm_base,\n          \"r_vp_base\": r_vp_base,\n          \"policy_gnorm_se_ln\": policy_gnorm_se_ln,\n          \"value_gnorm_se_ln\": value_gnorm_se_ln,\n          \"r_vp_se_ln\": r_vp_se_ln,\n          \"relative_r_vp_change\"\
    : (r_vp_se_ln - r_vp_base) / r_vp_base if r_vp_base != 'NaN' and r_vp_base != 0 else 'NaN',\n      }\n  \n      os.makedirs(\"storage/insight/results\", exist_ok=True)\n      path = f\"storage/insight/results/gradient_probe_rvp_tick_{int(time.time())}.json\" \n      with open(path, \"w\") as f:\n          json.dump(out, f, indent=2)\n      print(f\"DEBUG: {out}\")\n      print(f\"Wrote {path}\")\n      return out\n  \n  no_debugger: True\n```"
thinking_content: '**Developing a Mechanistic Probe for R_vp**


  Okay, so I''m aiming to build a new mechanistic probe, nestled within Private Memory, Capsule #14, that zeroes in on `R_vp`, the ratio of value to policy gradient norms. The game plan is to adapt the existing `ppo_sota_training_step` code to calculate and output these gradient norms in a dedicated `test()` function.


  The probe will operate like this: first, I''ll define a `test()` function. Within it, I''ll instantiate two versions of the network – the base Nomos II SOTA and the `ChannelAttention+LayerNorm` mitigated SOTA. I''ll initialize their parameters, probably with random weights to highlight architectural differences, though I might use pre-trained weights for another analysis if it becomes relevant. Then, I''ll whip up a synthetic batch of data, or, if possible, sample directly from the environment within the `test()` context.


  Next comes the core: defining a PPO `loss_fn` capable of returning the policy and value loss components separately, which is critical for calculating their individual gradient norms. I''ll compute the gradients for policy and value losses, then calculate the L2 norm for both the policy and value head gradients. Finally, I''ll calculate `R_vp` and store these metrics in a JSON file within lineage storage.


  I can reuse the existing `SingleStepWideLSTM_Base_ProbeNetwork` and `SingleStepWideLSTM_ChannelAttention_LayerNorm_ProbeNetwork` from previous capsules, which will be the input `network` parameter for calculating gradients in the `test()` function. The heart of the operation involves using `jax.value_and_grad` on the `loss_fn` – either separately for policy and value or within a combined `loss_fn` that isolates them. I''ll be drawing inspiration from `ppo_sota_training_step`, which already computes `policy_loss` and `value_loss`.


  The `test()` function itself needs refinement for calculating `R_vp`. I need to define separate functions, `policy_loss_only_fn` and `value_loss_only_fn`, to compute just those respective losses. After initializing the two networks, I''ll generate a dummy batch and compute both the losses and their gradients using `jax.value_and_grad`. The next challenge is extracting the policy and value head gradients. I''ll need to introspect into the parameter tree, much like Zephyr''s `_bucket_grad_norms` function. My target gradients would be those related to `Dense_2` and `Dense_3` layers if the Dense layers are unnamed, otherwise `policy_logits` and `value` respectively. Finally, I''ll calculate L2 norms and store the results.


  This probe will require a fair amount of detail. I''ll be sure to include the full code for `SqueezeExcitationBlock`, `ConvLSTMCellLN`, `BottleneckBlock`, and the two probe networks in the capsule. I''ll also need to include `calculate_gae` and parts of the `ppo_sota_training_step` for generating `advantages` and `returns` correctly, but I can probably simplify and use dummy values as in Zephyr''s probe, given the focus on gradient properties.


  Here is the update of the approach:

  Since the goal is `R_vp = ||∇L_v|| / ||∇L_p||`, the network used for gradient calculation in `test()` must produce `logits`, `values`, and `_`. I need `policy_logits` and `value` outputs. My current probe networks `SingleStepWideLSTM_Base_ProbeNetwork` and `SingleStepWideLSTM_ChannelAttention_LayerNorm_ProbeNetwork` only return `cnn_out`. So I need to modify them to output policy_logits and value (making them full networks).


  To make it easier, I will create `SingleStepWideLSTM_Base_ProbeNetwork_Full` and `SingleStepWideLSTM_ChannelAttention_LayerNorm_ProbeNetwork_Full` versions of the existing probes to make sure I am able to compute these gradients. I need both `policy_logits` and `value` outputs.


  Given the complexity, let''s simplify further. I should directly extract the parameters and gradients from the *full* network within the `test()` function, similar to Zephyr''s approach.


  So the refined `test()` function strategy is as follows:

  1.  Define a full `SingleStepWideLSTM` network (base) and a `SingleStepWideLSTM_ChannelAttention_LayerNorm` network (modified).

  2.  Initialize their parameters randomly with the same seed to isolate the architectural effect on gradients on *initialization*.

  3.  Create a synthetic batch of `obs`, `actions`,'
