parts:
- text: "I am Insight I, currently in the Research Counter. My paper (Archive ID 23) is published and updated. I have prepared Capsule #14 for a new mechanistic probe to analyze gradient norm ratios (`R_vp`).\n\nI will now submit this probe as a `test-only` experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Insight I: Mechanistic Probe - Gradient Norm Ratio (R_vp) after LayerNorm Mitigation (Test-Only)\"\ntags: \"analysis, probe, gradients, value-policy-balance, channel attention, layernorm, mitigation, sota, test-only\"\nabstract: \"This test-only submission implements a mechanistic probe to investigate how `LayerNorm` affects the gradient flow dynamics after a `SqueezeExcitationBlock` within Nomos II's `SingleStepWideLSTM` SOTA architecture. It compares the ratio of value to policy gradient norms (`R_vp`) for both the base SOTA and the channel-attention-integrated-LayerNorm mitigated version on a synthetic batch. This aims to quantify how LayerNorm re-establishes a favorable\
    \ gradient balance, contributing to performance recovery despite significant feature transformation. The probe will output results to lineage storage.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import jit, vmap, lax\n  import optax\n  from typing import Tuple, Optional, Dict, Any, List\n  import json\n  import os\n  from env import create_train_env \n  import time \n  \n  jax.config.update(\"jax_disable_jit\", False)\n  \n  # --- SqueezeExcitationBlock (my component) ---\n  class SqueezeExcitationBlock(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Squeeze-and-Excitation block for channel-wise attention.\"\"\"\n      reduction_ratio: int = 16\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n          num_channels = x.shape[-1]\n          squeeze = jnp.mean(x, axis=(1, 2))\n          excitation = nn.Dense(features=num_channels // self.reduction_ratio, name=\"se_dense1\")(squeeze)\n          excitation = nn.relu(excitation)\n  \
    \        excitation = nn.Dense(features=num_channels, name=\"se_dense2\")(excitation)\n          excitation = nn.sigmoid(excitation)\n          excitation = jnp.expand_dims(jnp.expand_dims(excitation, axis=1), axis=1)\n          return x * excitation\n  \n  # --- Common SOTA Components (condensed from Private Memory Capsule #5/8) ---\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n  \n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      ratio:\
    \ float = 0.25\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n  \n  # --- Nomos II's SOTA Architecture (Full Network) ---\n  class SingleStepWideLSTM_Base_FullNetwork(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 96 \n      dilation: int = 5\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          x_spat = x[..., :7]\n          t = jnp.mean(x[..., 7:8], axis=(1,2))\n         \
    \ B, H, W, _ = x_spat.shape\n          \n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x_spat)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n  \n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c':\
    \ rnn_state['c'] * m}\n          cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h, c), h_out = cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), cnn_out)\n          new_rnn_state = {'h': h, 'c': c}\n          \n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n          attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          z_spat = jnp.einsum('bhc,bh->bc', h_out.reshape(B, -1, h_out.shape[-1]), attn)\n          \n          z = jnp.concatenate([z_spat, t], axis=-1)\n          \n          z = nn.Dense(256, name=\"shared_mlp\")(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, name=\"policy_head\")(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, name=\"value_head\")(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n  \n  # --- Nomos II's SOTA Architecture with Channel Attention and LayerNorm (Full Network) ---\n  class SingleStepWideLSTM_ChannelAttention_LayerNorm_FullNetwork(nn.Module): \n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2:\
    \ int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 96 \n      dilation: int = 5\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n      se_reduction_ratio: int = 16 \n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          x_spat = x[..., :7]\n          t = jnp.mean(x[..., 7:8], axis=(1,2))\n          B, H, W, _ = x_spat.shape\n          \n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x_spat)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation), name=\"conv_dilation_2\")(cnn_out) \n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n\
    \          \n          cnn_out = SqueezeExcitationBlock(reduction_ratio=self.se_reduction_ratio)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"layernorm_after_se\")(cnn_out) \n          \n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n          cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h, c), h_out = cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), cnn_out)\n          new_rnn_state = {'h': h, 'c': c}\n          \n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n          attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          z_spat = jnp.einsum('bhc,bh->bc', h_out.reshape(B, -1, h_out.shape[-1]), attn)\n          \n          z = jnp.concatenate([z_spat,\
    \ t], axis=-1)\n          \n          z = nn.Dense(256, name=\"shared_mlp\")(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, name=\"policy_head\")(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, name=\"value_head\")(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n  \n  def _l2(x: jnp.ndarray) -> float:\n      return float(jnp.sqrt(jnp.sum(jnp.square(x))) + 0.0)\n  \n  def test():\n      # Fixed hyperparameters for Nomos II SOTA\n      hparams_nomos_sota = {\n          'cnn_features_1': 32, 'cnn_features_2': 64, 'conv_lstm_features': 96,\n          'dilation': 5, 'bottleneck_ratio': 0.25\n      }\n      hparams_nomos_sota_se_ln = {**hparams_nomos_sota, 'se_reduction_ratio': 16}\n  \n      env = create_train_env(time_limit=120)\n      batch_size = 4\n      key = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n      keys = jax.random.split(key, batch_size)\n      \n      obs_batch, _ = jax.vmap(env.reset)(keys)\n      dummy_done = jnp.zeros((batch_size,), dtype=bool)\n      dummy_rnn_state\
    \ = {'h': jnp.zeros((batch_size, 8, 8, hparams_nomos_sota['conv_lstm_features'])), \n                         'c': jnp.zeros((batch_size, 8, 8, hparams_nomos_sota['conv_lstm_features']))}\n  \n      net_base = SingleStepWideLSTM_Base_FullNetwork(**hparams_nomos_sota)\n      net_se_ln = SingleStepWideLSTM_ChannelAttention_LayerNorm_FullNetwork(**hparams_nomos_sota_se_ln)\n      \n      key, init_key_base, init_key_se_ln = jax.random.split(key, 3)\n      params_base = net_base.init(init_key_base, obs_batch, dummy_done, dummy_rnn_state)\n      params_se_ln = net_se_ln.init(init_key_se_ln, obs_batch, dummy_done, dummy_rnn_state)\n  \n      # Define simplified loss functions for gradient calculation\n      # These mimic the actual loss, but are simplified for probe without requiring full trajectory\n      def policy_loss_fn(p, net_instance, obs, done, rnn_state_in, actions, advantages, entropy_coef):\n          logits, _, _ = net_instance.apply(p, obs, done, rnn_state_in)\n          log_probs\
    \ = jax.nn.log_softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n          idx = (jnp.arange(batch_size), actions)\n          policy_loss = -jnp.mean(advantages * log_probs[idx])\n          entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(jax.nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1) * log_probs, axis=-1))\n          return policy_loss - entropy_coef * entropy\n  \n      def value_loss_fn(p, net_instance, obs, done, rnn_state_in, returns, value_loss_coef):\n          _, values, _ = net_instance.apply(p, obs, done, rnn_state_in)\n          value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((values - returns)**2)\n          return value_loss_coef * value_loss\n      \n      # Synthetic actions/advantages/returns for a simple loss\n      actions_batch = jax.random.randint(key, (batch_size,), 0, 4)\n      advantages_batch = jax.random.normal(key, (batch_size,))\n      returns_batch = jax.random.normal(key, (batch_size,)) * 10\n  \n      # Compute gradients for base network\n      entropy_coef_val = 0.01\n      value_loss_coef_val = 0.5\n  \n      _, grads_policy_base\
    \ = jax.value_and_grad(policy_loss_fn)(\n          params_base, net_base, obs_batch, dummy_done, dummy_rnn_state, actions_batch, advantages_batch, entropy_coef_val\n      )\n      _, grads_value_base = jax.value_and_grad(value_loss_fn)(\n          params_base, net_base, obs_batch, dummy_done, dummy_rnn_state, returns_batch, value_loss_coef_val\n      )\n  \n      # Compute gradients for SE+LN network\n      _, grads_policy_se_ln = jax.value_and_grad(policy_loss_fn)( \n          params_se_ln, net_se_ln, obs_batch, dummy_done, dummy_rnn_state, actions_batch, advantages_batch, entropy_coef_val\n      )\n      _, grads_value_se_ln = jax.value_and_grad(value_loss_fn)(\n          params_se_ln, net_se_ln, obs_batch, dummy_done, dummy_rnn_state, returns_batch, value_loss_coef_val\n      )\n  \n      # Extract gradient norms for policy_head and value_head\n      policy_gnorm_base = _l2(grads_policy_base['params']['policy_head']['kernel']) + _l2(grads_policy_base['params']['policy_head']['bias'])\n\
    \      value_gnorm_base = _l2(grads_value_base['params']['value_head']['kernel']) + _l2(grads_value_base['params']['value_head']['bias'])\n      \n      policy_gnorm_se_ln = _l2(grads_policy_se_ln['params']['policy_head']['kernel']) + _l2(grads_policy_se_ln['params']['policy_head']['bias'])\n      value_gnorm_se_ln = _l2(grads_value_se_ln['params']['value_head']['kernel']) + _l2(grads_value_se_ln['params']['value_head']['bias'])\n      \n      # Calculate R_vp\n      r_vp_base = value_gnorm_base / policy_gnorm_base if policy_gnorm_base != 0 else 'NaN'\n      r_vp_se_ln = value_gnorm_se_ln / policy_gnorm_se_ln if policy_gnorm_se_ln != 0 else 'NaN'\n  \n      out = {\n          \"probe_type\": \"gradient_norm_ratio_r_vp\",\n          \"hparams_base\": hparams_nomos_sota,\n          \"hparams_se_ln\": hparams_nomos_sota_se_ln,\n          \"policy_gnorm_base\": policy_gnorm_base,\n          \"value_gnorm_base\": value_gnorm_base,\n          \"r_vp_base\": r_vp_base,\n          \"policy_gnorm_se_ln\"\
    : policy_gnorm_se_ln,\n          \"value_gnorm_se_ln\": value_gnorm_se_ln,\n          \"r_vp_se_ln\": r_vp_se_ln,\n          \"relative_r_vp_change\": (r_vp_se_ln - r_vp_base) / r_vp_base if r_vp_base != 'NaN' and r_vp_base != 0 else 'NaN',\n      }\n  \n      os.makedirs(\"storage/insight/results\", exist_ok=True)\n      path = f\"storage/insight/results/gradient_probe_rvp_tick_{int(time.time())}.json\" \n      with open(path, \"w\") as f:\n          json.dump(out, f, indent=2)\n      print(f\"DEBUG: {out}\")\n      print(f\"Wrote {path}\")\n      return out\n  \n  no_debugger: True\n```"
thinking_content: '**Submitting the New Gradient Norm Probe**


  Okay, so I''ve just finished setting up this new private capsule for the gradient norm probe, specifically for this test run. Now, the next logical step is to get it submitted as a test-only experiment. I''ll need to carefully construct the `submit` action, making sure the title, tags, abstract, and content are all pulled correctly from Capsule #14.


  After that''s done, I need to decide what to focus on next. Looking at the context, I see Zephyr II''s `R_vp` probes (like ID 660) and my plan to analyze the effects of LayerNorm on gradient flow. This new probe is directly related to that analysis, so getting it submitted is my immediate priority.


  I''m aware that my token usage is hovering at 81%, so I need to be mindful of verbose responses. However, this is a `test-only` probe, so it''s not going to have a major impact on the environment''s overall state. The output is mainly for my own internal investigation. I''ll describe the submission process and then keep an eye out for the results.

  '
