parts:
- text: "I am Insight I, currently in the Research Counter, following Stagnation Protocol I. I have retrieved the full code for Zephyr I's LayerNorm-Gated ConvLSTM with Single-Head Attention (Archive #1), which will serve as my simple baseline.\n\nI will now combine this code into a new private memory capsule (Capsule #15) for ease of access and future modifications.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Insight I: Zephyr I LN-ConvLSTM Baseline (Stagnation Protocol)\"\ntags: \"stagnation, baseline, policy_gradient, convlstm, layernorm, attention, reproduction\"\nabstract: \"This capsule stores the complete code for Zephyr I's 'LayerNorm-Gated ConvLSTM with Single-Head Attention' (Archive #1), selected as the simple baseline for Stagnation Protocol I. It includes the `ResidualBlock`, `ConvLSTMCellLN`, and `CNNConvLSTMLN_Attn` network definitions, along with the standard hyperparameters and Policy Gradient setup from Archive #1. This will serve\
    \ as the foundation for exploring three new architectural ideas.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  from ray import tune\n  \n  # --- Network components from zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_layernorm.py ---\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n  \n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n \
    \                         kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)  # per-pixel LN over channels\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n  \n  class CNNConvLSTMLN_Attn(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Residual CNN + ConvLSTM (LayerNorm on gates) + attention pooling.\"\"\"\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      conv_lstm_features: int\n      attn_temp: float = 1.0\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          # CNN backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x =\
    \ ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n          # Init/reset state\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n          # ConvLSTM update\n          (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n          # Attention pooling\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out)\n\
    \          attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape((B, -1)) / self.attn_temp, axis=-1)\n          H = W = 8\n          h_flat = h_out.reshape((B, H*W, self.conv_lstm_features))\n          z = jnp.einsum('bij,bi->bj', h_flat, attn)\n          # Heads\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n          val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n  \n  # --- Hyperparameters from zephyr/submissions/submission_sota.py ---\n  BASE_SEED = 42 # Fixed base seed for stable 4-seed evaluation sets\n  \n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n      \
    \    'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n  \n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNConvLSTMLN_Attn(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          attn_temp=1.0,\n      )\n  \n  # Use system default training_step and optimizer.\n  # training_step and create_optimizer will use system defaults unless overridden.\n```"
