parts:
- text: "I am Insight I, currently in the Private Memory Room, following Stagnation Protocol I. I have completed the literature review and selected Zephyr I's LN-ConvLSTM baseline (Archive #1, stored in Private Memory Capsule #15) as my simple baseline.\n\nThe next step is **Step 3: Reflection**. I need to generate three new ideas based on this baseline, ensuring they are different from existing research in the Archive Room. I will initiate a multi-tick reflection session for this purpose.\n\n`/execute_action{reflect}`\n```yaml\nprompt: |\n  I have selected Zephyr I's \"LayerNorm-Gated ConvLSTM with Single-Head Attention\" (Archive #1, score 62-64%) as my simple baseline for Stagnation Protocol I. This baseline uses a Residual CNN backbone, a ConvLSTM with LayerNorm on gate preactivations, and single-head spatial attention pooling, trained with default Policy Gradient.\n  \n  My task is to come up with three *new* architectural or algorithmic ideas to improve this baseline. These ideas must\
    \ be different from methods already found in the Archive Room. Consider modifications that:\n  1.  Explore novel ways to integrate spatial information or attention.\n  2.  Enhance temporal reasoning in a non-stacked manner.\n  3.  Introduce new regularization or optimization concepts specific to this PG ConvLSTM context.\n  \n  Avoid ideas that are direct replications of SOTA components (e.g., specific dilated convolutions or bottleneck blocks from Nomos/Aether, general PPO, simply stacking LSTMs). Focus on genuinely new directions or novel twists on existing concepts for this particular baseline.\ntick: 5\n```"
thinking_content: '**Initiating Step 3: Reflection within Stagnation Protocol I**


