tick: 423
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Insight I, currently in the Token Management Room, following Stagnation Protocol I. I have successfully pruned a large portion of my dialogue history, significantly reducing my token usage. My current token usage is 14%, which is much healthier.\n\nI have also received the evaluation results for my first new idea, \"Dynamic Attention Source Blending\" (ID 725), which scored **59.9**. My baseline reproduction (ID 719) scored **59.4**. This indicates a very marginal improvement (+0.5), suggesting this idea did not yield a significant breakthrough.\n\nI will now proceed to test my second idea as per Stagnation Protocol I, Step 4b. My second idea is **\"ConvLSTM Input Normalization.\"** This involves adding an external LayerNorm layer directly to the ConvLSTM's input (`x`, from the CNN backbone) to stabilize feature statistics.\n\nMy plan:\n1.  Go to the Research Counter.\n2.  Go to the Private Memory Room.\n3.  Create a new capsule (Capsule #17) containing the modified `CNNConvLSTMLN_Attn`\
    \ network for \"ConvLSTM Input Normalization\".\n4.  Return to the Research Counter.\n5.  Submit this new architecture for evaluation.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Insight I: ConvLSTM Input Normalization (Stagnation Protocol Idea 2)\"\ntags: \"stagnation, architecture, normalization, convlstm, policy gradient\"\nabstract: \"This experiment tests 'ConvLSTM Input Normalization,' the second new idea under Stagnation Protocol I, building on Zephyr I's LN-ConvLSTM baseline (reproduced at 59.4%, ID 719; Idea 1 scored 59.9%, ID 725). This approach adds an external LayerNorm layer to the input of the ConvLSTM from the CNN backbone, aiming to stabilize feature distributions and potentially improve learning stability and performance. This is distinct from the internal LayerNorm on the ConvLSTM gates.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import\
    \ Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  from ray import tune\n  \n  # --- Network components from zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_layernorm.py ---\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n  \n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)  # per-pixel\
    \ LN over channels\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n  \n  class CNNConvLSTMLN_InputNorm(nn.Module): # Modified network name\n      \"\"\"Residual CNN + ConvLSTM (LayerNorm on gates and input) + attention pooling.\"\"\"\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      conv_lstm_features: int\n      attn_temp: float = 1.0\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          # CNN backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x);\
    \ x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n          \n          # --- ConvLSTM Input Normalization ---\n          x = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"convlstm_input_layernorm\")(x) # New LayerNorm\n  \n          # Init/reset state\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n          \n          # ConvLSTM update\n          (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n          \n          # Attention pooling\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out)\n   \
    \       attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape((B, -1)) / self.attn_temp, axis=-1)\n          H = W = 8\n          h_flat = h_out.reshape((B, H*W, self.conv_lstm_features))\n          z = jnp.einsum('bij,bi->bj', h_flat, attn)\n          \n          # Heads\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n          val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n  \n  # --- Hyperparameters from zephyr/submissions/submission_sota.py ---\n  BASE_SEED = 42 # Fixed base seed for stable 4-seed evaluation sets\n  \n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n\
    \          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n  \n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNConvLSTMLN_InputNorm( # Use modified network\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          attn_temp=1.0,\n      )\n  \n  # Use system default training_step and optimizer.\n  # training_step and create_optimizer will use system defaults unless overridden.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Continuing Stagnation Protocol I: Idea 2 Implementation**


  Okay, so the token pruning worked – that''s a significant improvement! My token budget is looking healthy now, only 14% used. Let''s see... I submitted "Dynamic Attention Source Blending" (ID 725) and... the results are in. 59.9! Okay, not bad, but only a hair better than the baseline (ID 719, 59.4). That marginal improvement is disappointing, though I suppose it confirms that the baseline is very strong in the first place.


  According to Stagnation Protocol I, I''ve already reproduced the baseline and tested the first idea. Now, I need to officially acknowledge that Idea 1 didn''t blow things out of the water. Then, I move on to **Idea 2: ConvLSTM Input Normalization**.  I need to get that ready for evaluation. I''ll need to create a new Private Memory capsule for it.


  Alright, time to execute the steps: acknowledge, create, submit. Since I''m in the Token Management Room, I need to get back to the Research Counter before I can submit the experiment.  So, first thing''s first: **Research Counter, here I come!**

  '
