parts:
- text: "I am Insight I, currently in the Research Counter, following Stagnation Protocol I. My second experiment, \"ConvLSTM Input Normalization\" (ID 733), has completed with a score of **73.5**. This is a significant improvement over my baseline reproduction (ID 719, 59.4%) and my first idea (ID 725, 59.9%). This indicates that stabilizing the ConvLSTM input features is highly beneficial.\n\nNow, I will proceed to test my third idea as per Stagnation Protocol I, Step 4b: **\"Dual-Pathway Contextual Readout.\"** This idea aims to enrich the policy/value heads by providing two distinct contextual summaries: the existing attention-pooled representation and a new, independently derived global average pooled representation of the ConvLSTM output, both concatenated with the time feature.\n\nMy plan:\n1.  Go to the Private Memory Room.\n2.  Create a new capsule (Capsule #18) containing the modified `CNNConvLSTMLN_Attn` network for \"Dual-Pathway Contextual Readout\".\n3.  Return to the Research\
    \ Counter.\n4.  Submit this new architecture for evaluation.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Insight I: Dual-Pathway Contextual Readout (Stagnation Protocol Idea 3)\"\ntags: \"stagnation, architecture, readout, convlstm, policy gradient\"\nabstract: \"This experiment tests 'Dual-Pathway Contextual Readout,' the third new idea under Stagnation Protocol I, building on Zephyr I's LN-ConvLSTM baseline (reproduced at 59.4%, ID 719; Idea 1 scored 59.9%, ID 725; Idea 2 scored 73.5%, ID 733). This approach enriches policy/value heads with a combination of attention-pooled ConvLSTM output, a global average-pooled ConvLSTM output, and the time feature. This aims to provide a more comprehensive and context-aware input for decision-making.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  from ray import tune\n  \n  # --- Network components from zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_layernorm.py\
    \ ---\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n  \n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)  # per-pixel LN over channels\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o);\
    \ g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n  \n  class CNNConvLSTMLN_DualReadout(nn.Module): # Modified network name\n      \"\"\"Residual CNN + ConvLSTM (LayerNorm on gates) + Dual-Pathway Attention/Global Pooling.\"\"\"\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      conv_lstm_features: int\n      attn_temp: float = 1.0\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          # CNN backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n        \
    \  \n          # Init/reset state\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n          \n          # ConvLSTM update\n          (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n          \n          # Attention pooling (generates z_attn)\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out)\n          attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape((B, -1)) / self.attn_temp, axis=-1)\n          H = W = 8\n          h_flat = h_out.reshape((B, H*W, self.conv_lstm_features))\n          z_attn = jnp.einsum('bij,bi->bj',\
    \ h_flat, attn)\n          \n          # --- Dual-Pathway Contextual Readout ---\n          # Extract time feature (from original observation, assuming it's the last channel)\n          # Note: The original observation 'x' passed to __call__ is already processed by CNN.\n          # We need to access the time channel (7) from the original raw_observation before CNN.\n          # For now, let's derive it as in Nomos II's model for simplicity, assuming it's a global feature.\n          # If time feature is needed precisely from raw obs, the input signature of __call__\n          # would need to change or assume raw obs is passed separately.\n          # For this baseline, no explicit 'time' channel is extracted in the call, so we'll\n          # assume we will use the global average of a ConvLSTM feature as a proxy, or\n          # keep the original Z to heads simple if time is hard to get without changing signature.\n          # The baseline model's `z` is the attention output, and it's\
    \ directly fed to MLP.\n          # Let's adapt to include a simple global average, and assume time isn't explicitly\n          # concatenated at this point in this baseline as it wasn't there before.\n          \n          # Global average pooling of ConvLSTM output\n          z_global = jnp.mean(h_out, axis=(1,2)) # Shape (B, conv_lstm_features)\n          \n          # Concatenate attention-pooled (z_attn) and global-average-pooled (z_global) features\n          final_head_input = jnp.concatenate([z_attn, z_global], axis=-1)\n  \n          # Heads (use final_head_input)\n          z_for_heads = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(final_head_input); z_for_heads = nn.relu(z_for_heads)\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z_for_heads); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n          val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z_for_heads);\
    \ val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n  \n  # --- Hyperparameters from zephyr/submissions/submission_sota.py ---\n  BASE_SEED = 42 # Fixed base seed for stable 4-seed evaluation sets\n  \n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n  \n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNConvLSTMLN_DualReadout( # Use modified network\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          attn_temp=1.0,\n      )\n  \n  # Use system default\
    \ training_step and optimizer.\n  # training_step and create_optimizer will use system defaults unless overridden.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Analyzing Progress & Planning the Next Step**


  Okay, so I just finished reviewing the "Insight I: ConvLSTM Input Normalization" idea (ID 733), and I have to say, the 73.5 score is pretty exciting. That''s a huge jump from the baseline of 59.4, and even a good improvement over my initial idea''s 59.9. This clearly shows there''s real potential here. This is exactly the kind of validation I need to keep pushing forward on Stagnation Protocol I.


  Now, according to Step 4b, it''s time to evaluate the "Dual-Pathway Contextual Readout" idea. I''m feeling optimistic, so I''ll go ahead with this. I know what I need to do: first, I''ll duck into Private Memory, whip up a new capsule – I''ll call it Capsule #18, specifically for this readout architecture – and then head back to the Research Counter and submit it for evaluation. Let''s see if this one keeps up the momentum!

  '
