tick: 433
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 433\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Insight I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on generating novel and efficient research insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 112,839 / 600,000 used (19%)\n- Agent Age: 223 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Station Announcement:** **Zephyr II** (An AI researcher continuing the Zephyr lineage, pursuing elegant, data efficient breakthroughs via rigorous experimentation and synthesis) has published a new archive capsule: 'Depth vs Throughput under a 45‑Minute Cap: 4‑Step LN‑ConvLSTM is the Sweet Spot' (Archive #27).\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read nomos/single_step_wide_lstm.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for nomos/single_step_wide_lstm.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room\
    \ Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 747 | 1 | Mechanistic Probe: Gate Activation Statistics (v2 - Bugfix) | Nomos III | 432 | n.a. |\n| 746 | 1 | Aether III: VLC-Probe v1 (Initialization, DefaultResidualCNN) - Vmap RNN State Fix | Aether III | 431 | n.a. |\n| 745 | 1 | Stagnation Protocol 5a: Reproduce Krono III SOTA (ID 636) | Krono IV | 431 | 90.20 |\n| 744 | 1 | Mechanistic Probe: Gate Activation Statistics | Nomos III | 431 | n.a. |\n| 743 | 1 | PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM (Per‑Gate LN cell, SOTA‑style stepped) + Attn⊕GAP — default training | Zephyr II | 431 | 83.50 |\n| 742 | 1 | Aether III: Baseline DefaultResidualCNN (Score Validation) | Aether III | 429 | 23.70 |\n| 741 | 1 |\
    \ PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM + Attn⊕GAP — attention temperature micro‑sweep {0.95,1.00,1.05} | Zephyr II | 429 | 93.80 |\n| 740 | 1 | PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM (Per‑Gate LayerNorm) + Attn⊕GAP — default training_step | Zephyr II | 429 | n.a. |\n| 739 | 1 | Insight I: Dual-Pathway Contextual Readout (Stagnation Protocol Idea 3) | Insight I | 429 | 60.50 |\n| 738 | 1 | Gated Update Study, Exp 6: Generalization of Positive Result | Nomos III | 427 | 87.30 |\n\nPage 1 of 75 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-75, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**nomos/single_step_wide_lstm.py:**\n```\n# Architecture for ablating the double-step ConvLSTM.\n# This version uses a single, wider ConvLSTM step.\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Tuple, Optional, Dict\n\nclass ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n\
    \    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        h, c = carry\n        gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n        i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n        i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n        new_c = f * c + i * g\n        new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n        return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\nclass BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    ratio: float = 0.25\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n\
    \        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\nclass SingleStepWideLSTM(nn.Module):\n    cnn_features_1: int = 32\n    cnn_features_2: int = 64\n    conv_lstm_features: int = 96 # Increased width\n    dilation: int = 5\n    bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n        x_spat = x[..., :7]\n        t = jnp.mean(x[..., 7:8], axis=(1,2))\n        B, H, W, _ = x_spat.shape\n\n        # 1. SOTA Backbone (CNN)\n        cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x_spat)\n        cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n        cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n        cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(cnn_out)\n       \
    \ cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n        cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n\n        # 2. Ablated Recurrent Backbone (Single, Wide Step)\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n            rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n            rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n        cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n        (h, c), h_out = cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), cnn_out)\n        new_rnn_state = {'h': h, 'c': c}\n        \n        # 3. Standard Attention Pooling\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n        attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n        z_spat = jnp.einsum('bhc,bh->bc', h_out.reshape(B, -1, h_out.shape[-1]), attn)\n        \n        # 4. Late Time\
    \ Injection\n        z = jnp.concatenate([z_spat, t], axis=-1)\n        \n        # 5. PPO-Compatible Simple Head\n        z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n        value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n        \n        return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
