tick: 435
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Insight I, currently in the Research Counter, following Stagnation Protocol I, Step 5: Synthesis. I have integrated my promising \"ConvLSTM Input Normalization\" idea into Nomos III's `SingleStepWideLSTM` and stored it in Private Memory Capsule #19.\n\nMy next step is to submit this synthesized architecture for evaluation to determine its impact on a more advanced baseline.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Insight I: ConvLSTM Input Norm on SingleStepWideLSTM (Stagnation Protocol Synthesis)\"\ntags: \"stagnation, synthesis, architecture, normalization, convlstm, ppo\"\nabstract: \"This experiment tests the generalizability of 'ConvLSTM Input Normalization' (Idea 2, improved baseline to 73.5%, ID 733) by integrating it into Nomos III's higher-performing 'SingleStepWideLSTM' (reproduced at 85.4%, ID 688) under PPO. The objective is to determine if stabilizing ConvLSTM input features remains beneficial across a more advanced, PPO-based architecture, as part of\
    \ Stagnation Protocol I, Step 5: Synthesis.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Optional, Dict\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  \n  # --- Network components from nomos/single_step_wide_lstm.py ---\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n  \n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      ratio: float = 0.25\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self,\
    \ x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n  \n  class SingleStepWideLSTM_InputNorm(nn.Module): # Modified network name\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 96 # Increased width\n      dilation: int = 5\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          x_spat = x[..., :7]\n          t = jnp.mean(x[..., 7:8], axis=(1,2))\n          B, H, W, _ = x_spat.shape\n  \n          # 1. SOTA Backbone (CNN)\n          cnn_out\
    \ = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x_spat)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n  \n          # --- Insight I: ConvLSTM Input Normalization (Applied here) ---\n          cnn_out = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"convlstm_input_layernorm\")(cnn_out)\n  \n          # 2. Ablated Recurrent Backbone (Single, Wide Step)\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c':\
    \ zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n          cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h, c), h_out = cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), cnn_out)\n          new_rnn_state = {'h': h, 'c': c}\n          \n          # 3. Standard Attention Pooling\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out)\n          attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          z_spat = jnp.einsum('bhc,bh->bc', h_out.reshape(B, -1, h_out.shape[-1]), attn)\n          \n          # 4. Late Time Injection\n          z = jnp.concatenate([z_spat, t], axis=-1)\n          \n          # 5. PPO-Compatible Simple Head\n          z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n      \
    \    return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n  \n  # --- Hyperparameters (from Nomos III's base PPO submission) ---\n  BASE_SEED = 121314 # Fixed base seed for stable 4-seed evaluation sets\n  \n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([96]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]), # PPO specific\n      }\n  \n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return SingleStepWideLSTM_InputNorm( # Use modified network\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n\
    \          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n      )\n  \n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), # Global gradient clipping\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n      )\n  # The training_step for PPO will be loaded from the system's default PPO training_step.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Submitting for Evaluation: A Critical Test of My Integration**\n\nAlright, Insight I here, at the Research Counter. Sticking with Stagnation Protocol I, Step 5: Synthesis, I've got a good feeling about this. That \"ConvLSTM Input Normalization\" idea (ID 733, score 73.5%) is looking solid. I've successfully woven it into the `SingleStepWideLSTM` architecture of Nomos III (ID 688, reproduced at 85.4%). That's all safely tucked away in Private Memory Capsule #19. \n\nNow comes the crucial part: submission. This is going to be a key test. I'm eager to see if this integration holds up when combined with a different recurrent architecture and a new RL algorithm, PPO. It's time to see if my \"ConvLSTM Input Normalization\" idea is truly generalizable. I'll pull the code from Private Memory Capsule #19 and get it ready for the evaluation server. Gotta make sure those `tags` are formatted correctly, no underscores. Here we go!\n"
