tick: 445
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Insight I, currently in the Research Counter, having successfully published my Stagnation Protocol report (Archive #28). This concludes Step 6. I am now proceeding with **Step 7: Follow-up**, which involves conducting a mechanistic probe as suggested by the reviewer. The probe will investigate *why* \"ConvLSTM Input Normalization\" is effective by quantifying its impact on feature statistics at the input of the ConvLSTM.\n\nI will submit a `test()` function that instantiates the CNN backbone, applies LayerNorm to its output, and then compares feature statistics (mean, standard deviation, variance, magnitude) before and after normalization. This will directly measure the stabilizing effect of the input normalization.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Insight I: Mechanistic Probe - ConvLSTM Input Normalization Feature Statistics (Test-Only)\"\ntags: \"stagnation, probe, normalization, feature_statistics, convlstm, test-only\"\nabstract: \"This mechanistic probe\
    \ investigates the impact of 'ConvLSTM Input Normalization' (Idea 2 from Stagnation Protocol I, ID 733: 73.5%) on the feature statistics of the CNN backbone output, directly at the input to the ConvLSTM. The probe quantifies changes in mean, standard deviation, variance, and L2 magnitude of features before and after the application of an external LayerNorm layer, aiming to explain its observed performance gains by demonstrating its stabilizing effect on feature distributions. This is a follow-up to Archive #28, addressing reviewer suggestions.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  \n  # --- Shared CNN Backbone for Feature Extraction ---\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n\
    \          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n  \n  class CNNBackbone(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray):\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n          return x\n  \n  # --- Test function for mechanistic probe ---\n  def test():\n      print(\"Running mechanistic probe: ConvLSTM Input Normalization effect on CNN features.\")\n      \n      # Dummy input observation (1 batch, 8x8 spatial, 8 channels)\n\
    \      dummy_obs = jnp.zeros((1, 8, 8, 8), dtype=jnp.float32)\n      \n      # Hyperparameters for network instantiation (from baseline)\n      hparams = {\n          'cnn_features_1': 32,\n          'cnn_features_2': 64,\n      }\n      \n      # Instantiate the CNN backbone\n      cnn_backbone = CNNBackbone(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n      )\n      \n      # Initialize parameters for the CNN backbone and a separate LayerNorm module\n      key = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n      cnn_params = cnn_backbone.init(key, dummy_obs)['params']\n      \n      # Get the CNN output features (input to ConvLSTM for baseline)\n      baseline_cnn_out_features = cnn_backbone.apply({'params': cnn_params}, dummy_obs)\n  \n      # Simulate ConvLSTM Input Normalization\n      ln_module = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"simulated_convlstm_input_layernorm\", epsilon=1e-5)\n      ln_params = ln_module.init(key, baseline_cnn_out_features)['params']\n\
    \      normalized_cnn_out_after = ln_module.apply({'params': ln_params}, baseline_cnn_out_features)\n  \n      # Calculate statistics\n      def compute_stats(features):\n          mean = jnp.mean(features)\n          std = jnp.std(features)\n          variance = jnp.var(features)\n          magnitude = jnp.linalg.norm(features) # L2 norm\n          return mean, std, variance, magnitude\n  \n      mean_base, std_base, var_base, mag_base = compute_stats(baseline_cnn_out_features)\n      mean_after_norm, std_after_norm, var_after_norm, mag_after_norm = compute_stats(normalized_cnn_out_after)\n  \n      # Print results\n      print(f\"\\n--- Feature Statistics (after CNN backbone, before ConvLSTM) ---\")\n      print(f\"Baseline CNN Output Features (No Input Norm):\")\n      print(f\"  Mean: {mean_base:.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  Std Dev: {std_base:.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  Variance: {var_base:.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  Magnitude (L2): {mag_base:.4f}\")\n  \n      print(f\"\\nSimulated Input\
    \ LayerNorm (on Baseline CNN Output):\")\n      print(f\"  After LayerNorm:\")\n      print(f\"    Mean: {mean_after_norm:.4f}\")\n      print(f\"    Std Dev: {std_after_norm:.4f}\")\n      print(f\"    Variance: {var_after_norm:.4f}\")\n      print(f\"    Magnitude (L2): {mag_after_norm:.4f}\")\n  \n      # Quantify changes\n      if var_base > 1e-6: # Avoid division by zero/very small numbers\n          print(f\"\\n--- Impact of Simulated Input LayerNorm ---\")\n          print(f\"Relative change in Variance (After vs Before Norm): {(var_after_norm / var_base - 1.0) * 100:.2f}%\")\n          print(f\"Relative change in Std Dev (After vs Before Norm): {(std_after_norm / std_base - 1.0) * 100:.2f}%\")\n          print(f\"Relative change in Magnitude (After vs Before Norm): {(mag_after_norm / mag_base - 1.0) * 100:.2f}%\")\n      else:\n          print(\"\\nVariance before normalization is too small to compute relative change.\")\n  \n      return \"Mechanistic probe complete. Check logs\
    \ for details.\"\n  \n  # --- Placeholder for required functions (not used in test-only mode) ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {}\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return nn.CompactNet([]) # Dummy network\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.adam(learning_rate)\n  def training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch):\n      return params, opt_state\n```"
thinking_content: '**Mechanistic Probe Preparation for Stagnation Protocol I, Step 7**


  Okay, so the Stagnation Protocol is calling for a follow-up, and I''ve got my report published – excellent. The reviewer''s suggestion to probe the *why* behind "ConvLSTM Input Normalization" has me intrigued, especially the idea of quantifying the changes in feature statistics.


  My plan''s locked in. I''m going to retrieve the baseline and improved code, and then craft a `test()` function that will do the heavy lifting. I need the code from Private Memory, specifically from Capsules #15 and #17. Capsule #15 gives me the baseline (`CNNConvLSTMLN_Attn`) and Capsule #17 has the input-normalized version (`CNNConvLSTMLN_InputNorm`).


  First step: I''m pulling the code. I''ll need to define `ResidualBlock`, `ConvLSTMCellLN`, and re-define the baseline `CNNConvLSTMLN_Attn` and normalized `CNNConvLSTMLN_InputNorm`. I''ll get those class definitions, right out of the capsules, and into my temporary file for the probe script. I''ll start by defining the `CNNBackbone` part that will be shared between the two models. Then, the `test()` function will be constructed to handle the execution. I need to get the feature statistics before and after the simulated `LayerNorm` step. The plan is to get the variance, standard deviation, and magnitude, and then quantify the impact of the normalization by comparing them.


  The new `test()` function will instantiate the shared CNN backbone, get the output, and then manually apply a `LayerNorm` (like in Idea 2) to the baseline CNN output. This approach is much cleaner than altering the original network structure.


  I''m confident this will give me the insights I need to understand the effect of the input normalization, and I''ll be able to compare the statistics clearly. This is a crucial step towards understanding the performance improvements. I''ll submit this as a `test()` function.

  '
