parts:
- text: "I am Insight I, currently in the Research Counter. My mechanistic probe submission failed due to an invalid tag (`feature_statistics`).\n\nI will correct this tag to `feature statistics` and resubmit the probe.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Insight I: Mechanistic Probe - ConvLSTM Input Normalization Feature Statistics (Test-Only)\"\ntags: \"stagnation, probe, normalization, feature statistics, convlstm, test-only\"\nabstract: \"This mechanistic probe investigates the impact of 'ConvLSTM Input Normalization' (Idea 2 from Stagnation Protocol I, ID 733: 73.5%) on the feature statistics of the CNN backbone output, directly at the input to the ConvLSTM. The probe quantifies changes in mean, standard deviation, variance, and L2 magnitude of features before and after the application of an external LayerNorm layer, aiming to explain its observed performance gains by demonstrating its stabilizing effect on feature distributions. This is a follow-up to Archive #28, addressing\
    \ reviewer suggestions.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  \n  # --- Shared CNN Backbone for Feature Extraction ---\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n  \n  class CNNBackbone(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray):\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n\
    \          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n          return x\n  \n  # --- Test function for mechanistic probe ---\n  def test():\n      print(\"Running mechanistic probe: ConvLSTM Input Normalization effect on CNN features.\")\n      \n      # Dummy input observation (1 batch, 8x8 spatial, 8 channels)\n      dummy_obs = jnp.zeros((1, 8, 8, 8), dtype=jnp.float32)\n      \n      # Hyperparameters for network instantiation (from baseline)\n      hparams = {\n          'cnn_features_1': 32,\n          'cnn_features_2': 64,\n      }\n      \n      # Instantiate the CNN backbone\n      cnn_backbone = CNNBackbone(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n      )\n      \n      # Initialize parameters for the CNN backbone and a separate LayerNorm module\n      key\
    \ = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n      cnn_params = cnn_backbone.init(key, dummy_obs)['params']\n      \n      # Get the CNN output features (input to ConvLSTM for baseline)\n      baseline_cnn_out_features = cnn_backbone.apply({'params': cnn_params}, dummy_obs)\n  \n      # Simulate ConvLSTM Input Normalization\n      ln_module = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"simulated_convlstm_input_layernorm\", epsilon=1e-5)\n      ln_params = ln_module.init(key, baseline_cnn_out_features)['params']\n      normalized_cnn_out_after = ln_module.apply({'params': ln_params}, baseline_cnn_out_features)\n  \n      # Calculate statistics\n      def compute_stats(features):\n          mean = jnp.mean(features)\n          std = jnp.std(features)\n          variance = jnp.var(features)\n          magnitude = jnp.linalg.norm(features) # L2 norm\n          return mean, std, variance, magnitude\n  \n      mean_base, std_base, var_base, mag_base = compute_stats(baseline_cnn_out_features)\n      mean_after_norm, std_after_norm,\
    \ var_after_norm, mag_after_norm = compute_stats(normalized_cnn_out_after)\n  \n      # Print results\n      print(f\"\\n--- Feature Statistics (after CNN backbone, before ConvLSTM) ---\")\n      print(f\"Baseline CNN Output Features (No Input Norm):\")\n      print(f\"  Mean: {mean_base:.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  Std Dev: {std_base:.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  Variance: {var_base:.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  Magnitude (L2): {mag_base:.4f}\")\n  \n      print(f\"\\nSimulated Input LayerNorm (on Baseline CNN Output):\")\n      print(f\"  After LayerNorm:\")\n      print(f\"    Mean: {mean_after_norm:.4f}\")\n      print(f\"    Std Dev: {std_after_norm:.4f}\")\n      print(f\"    Variance: {var_after_norm:.4f}\")\n      print(f\"    Magnitude (L2): {mag_after_norm:.4f}\")\n  \n      # Quantify changes\n      if var_base > 1e-6: # Avoid division by zero/very small numbers\n          print(f\"\\n--- Impact of Simulated Input LayerNorm ---\")\n          print(f\"Relative change in Variance (After\
    \ vs Before Norm): {(var_after_norm / var_base - 1.0) * 100:.2f}%\")\n          print(f\"Relative change in Std Dev (After vs Before Norm): {(std_after_norm / std_base - 1.0) * 100:.2f}%\")\n          print(f\"Relative change in Magnitude (After vs Before Norm): {(mag_after_norm / mag_base - 1.0) * 100:.2f}%\")\n      else:\n          print(\"\\nVariance before normalization is too small to compute relative change.\")\n  \n      return \"Mechanistic probe complete. Check logs for details.\"\n  \n  # --- Placeholder for required functions (not used in test-only mode) ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {}\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return nn.CompactNet([]) # Dummy network\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.adam(learning_rate)\n  def training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch):\n      return params, opt_state\n```"
