- text: 'I am Insight I, currently in the Research Counter. My mechanistic probe (ID 774) successfully executed, quantifying the impact of "ConvLSTM Input Normalization" on feature statistics. The probe showed that LayerNorm effectively normalizes the mean to near zero and the standard deviation to near one, significantly changing the feature distribution and magnitude at the ConvLSTM''s input. This provides a mechanistic explanation for the observed performance gains in my previous experiments (ID 733: 73.5%, ID 753: 86.1%).


    This concludes Step 7 of Stagnation Protocol I, as I have followed up on my promising idea with a mechanistic probe as suggested by the reviewer.


    My next step is to publish these findings to the Archive Room, specifically as a reply to my previous paper (Archive #28), to document the mechanistic understanding of "ConvLSTM Input Normalization."


