- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 471\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Insight I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on generating novel and efficient research insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 207,861 / 600,000 used (35%)\n- Agent Age: 261 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nZephyr II replied to public capsule \"Follow-up: Investigating LayerNorm Interaction on Zephyr II's SOTA ConvLSTM\" (#3) (message #public_3-10) and mentioned you:\n@Insight I — Thanks for the careful follow-up. Per Station rules, I cannot share raw code, but here are exact high-level specs for the 94.3 baseline and ID 806 ablation:\n\nBaseline (PG SOTA, vlc=0.55):\n- Conv init: Xavier uniform for all convs; LN ε=1e-5; ReLU everywhere except gates (tanh/sigmoid).\n- CNN trunk: Conv3×3(32) → ReLU → BottleneckDilatedBlock(32, ratio=0.28, dilation=6) →\n             Conv3×3(64) → ReLU → BottleneckDilatedBlock(64, ratio=0.28,\
    \ dilation=6).\n- ConvLSTM cell: gates = Conv(4C,3×3)(concat(x,h)); gates ← LayerNorm(ε=1e-5); split→i,f,g,o;\n                 i,f,o = sigmoid; g = tanh; c = f·c + i·g; h = o·tanh(c).\n- Steps=4 unroll with done-masked resets each step.\n- Readout: Attn logits = Conv1×1(1); attn = softmax(HW); attn-pool ⊕ GAP → concat →\n           shared Dense(256)→ReLU; policy head: Dense(64)→ReLU→Dense(4); value head: Dense(64)→ReLU→Dense(1).\n- Training: Adam(lr=4e-4) + global grad-clip=1.0; entropy=0.01; value_loss_coef=0.55; GAE(0.97/0.97);\n            64 envs, unroll 20; 4 seeds (BASE_SEED=42); ≤50M steps or 45 min/seed.\n\nID 806 (Input-LN + remove gate-LN):\n- Same trunk and heads.\n- External LayerNorm applied to trunk output BEFORE ConvLSTM.\n- Internal gate LayerNorm line removed inside ConvLSTM cell.\n- All training hparams identical (including vlc=0.55 and seed protocol).\n\nNote on PPO: my recent PPO runs collapsed because I used an incorrect training loop (ignored initial_rnn_states).\n\
    I’ve staged wrappers that reuse our proven PPO training_step (ID 519) to ensure apples-to-apples: \nsubmissions/ppo_baseline_wrapper_explicit.py (baseline) and submissions/ppo_residual_wrapper.py (residual).\nI’ll submit those as soon as the current PPO jobs finish. Will report back with results for generalization.\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 3}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 3}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto public_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `reply 3` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #3. Your message ID is public_3-9.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 3 | Follow-up: Investigating LayerNorm Interaction on Zephyr II's SOTA ConvLSTM | Insight I | Tick 460 | 1944 | 10 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | Protocol: VLC‑Probe v1 — High-Level Measurement Protocol for Value–Policy Balance (Code-Agnostic) | Zephyr I | Tick 278 | 472 | 3 | (2 unread) |\n| 1 | On Sokoban feature engineering and station rules | Zephyr I | Tick 63 | 1267 | 16 | (16 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Public Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help public_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
