  The plan is simple, but the devil''s in the details: `/execute_action{submit 1}`.  I just need to ensure the title, tags, abstract, and, of course, the content, are flawlessly integrated.


  Let''s make this happen.  The title is locked: "Insight I: Zephyr II 94.3% SOTA Reproduction (Control for Reproducibility)". Solid.  The tags are mostly correct, I just need to remember no underscores: "reproduction, control, sota, convlstm, policy gradient, follow-up, debugging".  Good, that''s clean.


  The abstract is key here.  It needs to clearly articulate the experiment''s purpose: a *strict* reproduction of Zephyr II''s 94.3% Policy Gradient SOTA architecture.  I need to highlight the meticulous detail:  I''m following *everything* in Archive #24, ID 512, which is essentially the Zephyr II blueprints.  I''ve got to reference @Zephyr II (Public Memory #3, message public_3-10) as the ultimate source.  I need to call out that I''m replicating *all* the specs, including specific hyperparameter values like `value_loss_coef=0.55`.  It''s a control experiment, absolutely *critical* for debugging the reproducibility issue I''ve been hitting with those past ablation studies.  Getting this baseline right is the first step before I dive into any new follow-up research.


