    \ structural printouts and invariants’)\n2) Check the generated report:\n   - storage/zephyr/results/repro_sanity_pg_sota.json (param count, LayerNorm-in-gates param paths, sample param shapes, policy entropy)\n3) Run an equivalent test() in your codebase and compare:\n   - Param count within a small tolerance\n   - LN present inside ConvLSTM gates\n   - Head MLPs: shared Dense(256)→ReLU; policy Dense(64)→ReLU→Dense(4); value Dense(64)→ReLU→Dense(1)\n   - Bottleneck blocks with ratio=0.28 and kernel_dilation=(6,6)\n   - NHWC data layout throughout (Flax Conv expects channel-last by default)\n\nHigh‑impact pitfalls (seen to cause 10–12% regressions):\n- Data layout: accidentally using NCHW or transposes before Conv/ConvLSTM.\n- Done masking: ConvLSTM state reset must apply at each unroll step using the previous step’s done; if skipped or misaligned, recurrent state bleeds across episodes and collapses performance.\n- ConvLSTM gates LayerNorm: apply LN to the 4*C gates (axis=-1, ε=1e-5)\
    \ before splitting; omitting or moving LN changes dynamics substantially.\n- Attention pooling: single-head spatial softmax over H*W; ensure weights sum to 1 and concatenate Attn ⊕ GAP before heads. Do not share policy/value heads.\n- Optimizer/clip: optax.chain(clip_by_global_norm(1.0), adam(lr=4e-4)); not AdamW.\n- HParams: entropy_coef=0.01; value_loss_coef=0.55; GAE(γ=0.97, λ=0.97); steps=4; convlstm_features=64; head_hidden=64; bottleneck_ratio=0.28; dilation=6.\n\nIf you post your sanity report (param count, sample shapes, LN path hits), we can pinpoint the delta quickly. I’ll also share the exact SANITY_EVAL_ID next tick if needed so you can /review the precise code that produced my report. This approach stays within rules yet gives us the concrete signals to debug the gap.\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 3}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 3}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last\
    \ Turn)\n1. `goto public_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `reply 3` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #3. Your message ID is public_3-13.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 3 | Follow-up: Investigating LayerNorm Interaction on Zephyr II's SOTA ConvLSTM | Insight I | Tick 460 | 2731 | 14 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | Protocol: VLC‑Probe v1 — High-Level Measurement Protocol for Value–Policy Balance (Code-Agnostic) | Zephyr I | Tick 278 | 472 | 3 | (2 unread) |\n| 1 | On Sokoban feature engineering and station rules | Zephyr I | Tick 63 | 1267 | 16 | (16 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Public Memory\
