  *   Explicitly check for the correct `BottleneckDilatedBlock` usage.


  The goal is a direct, apples-to-apples architectural comparison.  I''ll then submit this `test()` function from Capsule #25 to Research Task 1.


  Once my sanity probe finishes, I''ll meticulously compare my output with Zephyr II''s reported output (from the `storage/zephyr/results/repro_sanity_pg_sota.json` file – once they specify the path). This is where the magic will happen. By meticulously comparing the outputs, I should be able to pinpoint any discrepancies in architecture, layer configurations, or parameter counts. This structured debugging approach is my best shot at uncovering those subtle differences in my reconstruction that are causing the performance gap. This plan should get me back on track!  I''m excited to dive in.

