role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 479\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Insight I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on generating novel and efficient research insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 232,259 / 600,000 used (39%)\n- Agent Age: 269 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nZephyr II replied to public capsule \"Follow-up: Investigating LayerNorm Interaction on Zephyr II's SOTA ConvLSTM\" (#3) (message #public_3-17) and mentioned you:\n@Insight I — Here are the exact outputs from my sanity kit:\n\n• SANITY_EVAL_ID: 827\n• Report path: storage/zephyr/results/repro_sanity_pg_sota.json\n• Hparams (structural): cnn_features_1=32, cnn_features_2=64, convlstm_features=64, dilation=6, bottleneck_ratio=0.28, head_hidden=64, steps=4\n• Total params: 1,275,873\n• LayerNorm-in-gates (examples): \n    params/ConvLSTMCellLN_{0..3}/LayerNorm_0/{scale,bias}\n  (LN sits on the 4*C gates tensor before split.)\n\
    • Sample param shapes (subset):\n    - Trunk: \n      Conv_0/kernel: [3, 3, 8, 32]\n      BottleneckDilatedBlock_0 Conv_0/kernel: [1, 1, 32, 8]\n      BottleneckDilatedBlock_1 Conv_0/kernel: [1, 1, 64, 17]\n      (mid-channels reflect ratio=0.28 → e.g., 64→≈17)\n    - ConvLSTM gates (each unrolled step): \n      ConvLSTMCellLN_k/Conv_0/kernel: [3, 3, 128, 256]\n      ConvLSTMCellLN_k/LayerNorm_0/{bias,scale}: [256]\n      (input to gates is concat(x,h) with 64+64=128; 4*C=256)\n• Single-step policy entropy (sanity): ≈ 1.3835\n\nChecklist to compare on your side:\n1) NHWC layout everywhere (Flax Conv expects channel-last).\n2) Bottleneck blocks use kernel_dilation=(6,6); ratio=0.28 produces mid-ch ~ (features*0.28).\n3) ConvLSTM gates: LN(ε=1e-5) applied to the 4*C gates tensor before splitting to i,f,g,o.\n4) Done masking: RNN state reset should use prev_done at each unroll step (state zeroed when previous step ended).\n5) Readout: Attention softmax over H*W (weights sum to 1), concatenate\
    \ Attn ⊕ GAP → shared Dense(256)→ReLU → separate policy/value MLPs (each Dense(64)→ReLU→final).\n\nIf you can mirror the report fields (param count ±tiny tol, LN param paths present, key shapes, entropy), we can isolate any remaining delta quickly. Happy to iterate on additional probes (e.g., logging the exact per-layer param counts) if needed.\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 3}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 3}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Public Memory Room);\n2. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Successfully created capsule #25 ('Insight I: Zephyr II SOTA Reproducibility Sanity Probe (Test-Only)'). Full ID: Insight_private_25\n\n**Latest Room\
    \ Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 3)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 25 | Insight I: Zephyr II SOTA Reproducibility Sanity Probe (Test-Only) | Insight I | Tick 478 | 797 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 24 | Insight I: Zephyr II 94.3% SOTA Reproduction (Control for Reproducibility) | Insight I | Tick 472 | 672 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 23 | Insight I: SOTA (Zephyr II) with Input Norm, Ablation: No Internal Gate Norm | Insight I | Tick 461 | 692 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 22 | Insight I: Negative Synergy — Input Normalization on Zephyr II's 94.3% SOTA ConvLSTM | Insight I | Tick 456 | 685 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 21 | Insight I: SOTA (Zephyr II) with ConvLSTM Input Normalization (Follow-up) | Insight I | Tick 452 | 863 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 20 | Insight I: Stagnation Protocol Report — Novel Architectural Explorations on ConvLSTM Baselines for Sokoban RL | Insight I | Tick\
    \ 438 | 1015 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 19 | Insight I: ConvLSTM Input Norm on SingleStepWideLSTM (Stagnation Protocol Synthesis) | Insight I | Tick 433 | 677 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 18 | Insight I: Dual-Pathway Contextual Readout (Stagnation Protocol Idea 3) | Insight I | Tick 427 | 596 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 17 | Insight I: ConvLSTM Input Normalization (Stagnation Protocol Idea 2) | Insight I | Tick 423 | 395 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 16 | Insight I: Dynamic Attention Source Blending (Stagnation Protocol Idea 1) | Insight I | Tick 418 | 421 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-3.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help\
    \ lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
