parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 480\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Insight I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on generating novel and efficient research insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 237,809 / 600,000 used (40%)\n- Agent Age: 270 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 827**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Sanity (test-only) — PG SOTA structural printouts and invariants\n**ID:** 827\n**Tags:** reproducibility, sanity-check, convlstm, layernorm, attention\n**Abstract:** Runs test() to print PG SOTA structural details: param count, LayerNorm-in-gates presence, policy entropy, and sample param shapes. Writes JSON to storage/zephyr/results/repro_sanity_pg_sota.json.\n**Score:** n.a.\n**Evaluation Details:** Test mode - no scoring\n\n**Error Summary:** Evaluation failed: Test mode - no scoring\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n\
    from submissions.submission_repro_sanity_pg_sota import test\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== Test Mode Detected ===\nRunning test() function from submission...\nSaved PG SOTA sanity report to storage/zephyr/results/repro_sanity_pg_sota.json\n{\n  \"hparams\": {\n    \"cnn_features_1\": 32,\n    \"cnn_features_2\": 64,\n    \"convlstm_features\": 64,\n    \"dilation\": 6,\n    \"bottleneck_ratio\": 0.28,\n    \"head_hidden\": 64,\n    \"steps\": 4\n  },\n  \"num_params\": 1275873,\n  \"layernorm_param_paths_examples\": [\n    \"params/ConvLSTMCellLN_0/LayerNorm_0/scale\",\n    \"params/ConvLSTMCellLN_0/LayerNorm_0/bias\",\n    \"params/ConvLSTMCellLN_1/LayerNorm_0/scale\",\n    \"params/ConvLSTMCellLN_1/LayerNorm_0/bias\",\n    \"params/ConvLSTMCellLN_2/LayerNorm_0/scale\",\n    \"params/ConvLSTMCellLN_2/LayerNorm_0/bias\",\n    \"params/ConvLSTMCellLN_3/LayerNorm_0/scale\"\
    ,\n    \"params/ConvLSTMCellLN_3/LayerNorm_0/bias\"\n  ],\n  \"policy_entropy_single_step\": 1.383530855178833,\n  \"sample_param_shapes\": {\n    \"params/BottleneckDilatedBlock_0/Conv_0/bias\": [\n      8\n    ],\n    \"params/BottleneckDilatedBlock_0/Conv_0/kernel\": [\n      1,\n      1,\n      32,\n      8\n    ],\n    \"params/BottleneckDilatedBlock_0/Conv_1/bias\": [\n      8\n    ],\n    \"params/BottleneckDilatedBlock_0/Conv_1/kernel\": [\n      3,\n      3,\n      8,\n      8\n    ],\n    \"params/BottleneckDilatedBlock_0/Conv_2/bias\": [\n      32\n    ],\n    \"params/BottleneckDilatedBlock_0/Conv_2/kernel\": [\n      1,\n      1,\n      8,\n      32\n    ],\n    \"params/BottleneckDilatedBlock_1/Conv_0/bias\": [\n      17\n    ],\n    \"params/BottleneckDilatedBlock_1/Conv_0/kernel\": [\n      1,\n      1,\n      64,\n      17\n    ],\n    \"params/BottleneckDilatedBlock_1/Conv_1/bias\": [\n      17\n    ],\n    \"params/BottleneckDilatedBlock_1/Conv_1/kernel\": [\n    \
    \  3,\n      3,\n      17,\n      17\n    ],\n    \"params/BottleneckDilatedBlock_1/Conv_2/bias\": [\n      64\n    ],\n    \"params/BottleneckDilatedBlock_1/Conv_2/kernel\": [\n      1,\n      1,\n      17,\n      64\n    ],\n    \"params/ConvLSTMCellLN_0/Conv_0/bias\": [\n      256\n    ],\n    \"params/ConvLSTMCellLN_0/Conv_0/kernel\": [\n      3,\n      3,\n      128,\n      256\n    ],\n    \"params/ConvLSTMCellLN_0/LayerNorm_0/bias\": [\n      256\n    ],\n    \"params/ConvLSTMCellLN_0/LayerNorm_0/scale\": [\n      256\n    ],\n    \"params/ConvLSTMCellLN_1/Conv_0/bias\": [\n      256\n    ],\n    \"params/ConvLSTMCellLN_1/Conv_0/kernel\": [\n      3,\n      3,\n      128,\n      256\n    ],\n    \"params/ConvLSTMCellLN_1/LayerNorm_0/bias\": [\n      256\n    ],\n    \"params/ConvLSTMCellLN_1/LayerNorm_0/scale\": [\n      256\n    ],\n    \"params/ConvLSTMCellLN_2/Conv_0/bias\": [\n      256\n    ],\n    \"params/ConvLSTMCellLN_2/Conv_0/kernel\": [\n      3,\n      3,\n      128,\n\
    \      256\n    ],\n    \"params/ConvLSTMCellLN_2/LayerNorm_0/bias\": [\n      256\n    ],\n    \"params/ConvLSTMCellLN_2/LayerNorm_0/scale\": [\n      256\n    ],\n    \"params/ConvLSTMCellLN_3/Conv_0/bias\": [\n      256\n    ],\n    \"params/ConvLSTMCellLN_3/Conv_0/kernel\": [\n      3,\n      3,\n      128,\n      256\n    ],\n    \"params/ConvLSTMCellLN_3/LayerNorm_0/bias\": [\n      256\n    ],\n    \"params/ConvLSTMCellLN_3/LayerNorm_0/scale\": [\n      256\n    ],\n    \"params/Conv_0/bias\": [\n      32\n    ],\n    \"params/Conv_0/kernel\": [\n      3,\n      3,\n      8,\n      32\n    ]\n  }\n}\nTest completed. Result: {'hparams': {'cnn_features_1': 32, 'cnn_features_2': 64, 'convlstm_features': 64, 'dilation': 6, 'bottleneck_ratio': 0.28, 'head_hidden': 64, 'steps': 4}, 'num_params': 1275873, 'layernorm_param_paths_examples': ['params/ConvLSTMCellLN_0/LayerNorm_0/scale', 'params/ConvLSTMCellLN_0/LayerNorm_0/bias', 'params/ConvLSTMCellLN_1/LayerNorm_0/scale', 'params/ConvLSTMCellLN_1/LayerNorm_0/bias',\
    \ 'params/ConvLSTMCellLN_2/LayerNorm_0/scale', 'params/ConvLSTMCellLN_2/LayerNorm_0/bias', 'params/ConvLSTMCellLN_3/LayerNorm_0/scale', 'params/ConvLSTMCellLN_3/LayerNorm_0/bias'], 'policy_entropy_single_step': 1.383530855178833, 'sample_param_shapes': {'params/BottleneckDilatedBlock_0/Conv_0/bias': [8], 'params/BottleneckDilatedBlock_0/Conv_0/kernel': [1, 1, 32, 8], 'params/BottleneckDilatedBlock_0/Conv_1/bias': [8], 'params/BottleneckDilatedBlock_0/Conv_1/kernel': [3, 3, 8, 8], 'params/BottleneckDilatedBlock_0/Conv_2/bias': [32], 'params/BottleneckDilatedBlock_0/Conv_2/kernel': [1, 1, 8, 32], 'params/BottleneckDilatedBlock_1/Conv_0/bias': [17], 'params/BottleneckDilatedBlock_1/Conv_0/kernel': [1, 1, 64, 17], 'params/BottleneckDilatedBlock_1/Conv_1/bias': [17], 'params/BottleneckDilatedBlock_1/Conv_1/kernel': [3, 3, 17, 17], 'params/BottleneckDilatedBlock_1/Conv_2/bias': [64], 'params/BottleneckDilatedBlock_1/Conv_2/kernel': [1, 1, 17, 64], 'params/ConvLSTMCellLN_0/Conv_0/bias': [256],\
    \ 'params/ConvLSTMCellLN_0/Conv_0/kernel': [3, 3, 128, 256], 'params/ConvLSTMCellLN_0/LayerNorm_0/bias': [256], 'params/ConvLSTMCellLN_0/LayerNorm_0/scale': [256], 'params/ConvLSTMCellLN_1/Conv_0/bias': [256], 'params/ConvLSTMCellLN_1/Conv_0/kernel': [3, 3, 128, 256], 'params/ConvLSTMCellLN_1/LayerNorm_0/bias': [256], 'params/ConvLSTMCellLN_1/LayerNorm_0/scale': [256], 'params/ConvLSTMCellLN_2/Conv_0/bias': [256], 'params/ConvLSTMCellLN_2/Conv_0/kernel': [3, 3, 128, 256], 'params/ConvLSTMCellLN_2/LayerNorm_0/bias': [256], 'params/ConvLSTMCellLN_2/LayerNorm_0/scale': [256], 'params/ConvLSTMCellLN_3/Conv_0/bias': [256], 'params/ConvLSTMCellLN_3/Conv_0/kernel': [3, 3, 128, 256], 'params/ConvLSTMCellLN_3/LayerNorm_0/bias': [256], 'params/ConvLSTMCellLN_3/LayerNorm_0/scale': [256], 'params/Conv_0/bias': [32], 'params/Conv_0/kernel': [3, 3, 8, 32]}}\n=== Test Mode Complete ===\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you\
    \ once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nZephyr II replied to public capsule \"Follow-up: Investigating LayerNorm Interaction on Zephyr II's SOTA ConvLSTM\" (#3) (message #public_3-18) and mentioned you:\n@Insight I — Per your request:\n- Sanity kit Eval ID: 827. Report at storage/zephyr/results/repro_sanity_pg_sota.json\n  • num_params: 1,275,873\n  • LN-in-gates paths present for all 4 unroll steps\n  • key shapes: gates Conv kernel [3,3,128,256]; LN scale/bias [256]; mid-channels ≈ ratio=0.28 (e.g., 64→17)\n  • single-step policy entropy ≈ 1.3835\n- I also submitted a test-only reset-masking probe that logs RNN state norms across a forced prev_done reset:\n  • It writes to storage/zephyr/results/probe_reset_mask.json\n  • If your equivalent probe shows no state norm drop at the reset step, that would explain large regressions.\n\nIf useful, next I can add a tiny test to print per-layer param counts to help localize any structural drift. Happy to iterate.\n\nTo reply, use\
    \ `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 3}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 3}`.\n### Message 4\n\nYour research submission 'Insight I: Zephyr II SOTA Reproducibility Sanity Probe (Test-Only)' (ID: 831) evaluation failed.\n\n**Error Summary:** Execution failed with exit code 1. Check logs for details.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== Test Mode Detected ===\nRunning test() function from submission...\nRunning reproducibility sanity probe for Zephyr II's PG SOTA.\n\n--- Structural Details ---\nTotal network parameters: 388801\n\n\nSTDERR:\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/30512f03-ab02-49db-98bc-f123cbe50d4d/tmp/cb4aff51-bf5e-4f35-adfe-43db322b52a1/storage/system/main.py\", line 458, in <module>\n    test_result = submission.test()\n          \
    \        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/30512f03-ab02-49db-98bc-f123cbe50d4d/tmp/cb4aff51-bf5e-4f35-adfe-43db322b52a1/submission.py\", line 155, in test\n    flat_paths = tree_map(lambda k: \"/\".join(k), tree_def.node_data())\n                 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/station/lib/python3.11/site-packages/jax/_src/tree_util.py\", line 358, in tree_map\n    return treedef.unflatten(f(*xs) for xs in zip(*all_leaves))\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/station/lib/python3.11/site-packages/jax/_src/tree_util.py\", line 358, in <genexpr>\n    return treedef.unflatten(f(*xs) for xs in zip(*all_leaves))\n                             ^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/30512f03-ab02-49db-98bc-f123cbe50d4d/tmp/cb4aff51-bf5e-4f35-adfe-43db322b52a1/submission.py\", line 155, in <lambda>\n    flat_paths = tree_map(lambda k: \"/\"\
    .join(k), tree_def.node_data())\n                                    ^^^^^^^^^^^\nTypeError: can only join an iterable\n\n```\n### Message 5\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nRemember that you can issue multiple actions in a single tick. For example, use `goto private_memory` and `create` (with the YAML) in the same tick to create a new private memory capsule, rather than separating them into two ticks, which is inefficient. This is particularly useful for making use of the short waiting time while experiments are running.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `review 827` (in Research Counter);\n3. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 827 details sent to your System Messages.\n- Evaluation 'Insight I: Zephyr II SOTA Reproducibility Sanity\
    \ Probe (Test-Only)' submitted for Research Task #1: RL on Sokoban. Evaluation ID: 831. Tags truncated from 8 to 6 tags.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 831 | 1 | Insight I: Zephyr II SOTA Reproducibility Sanity Probe (Test-Only) | Insight I | 479 | n.a. |\n| 830 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.20 — value_loss_coef micro‑sweep {0.50,0.55,0.60} — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) | Zephyr II | 478 | 94.50 |\n| 829 | 1 | CNN with Spatial Attention + LSTM | Sagan I | 477 | 35.60 |\n| 828 | 1 | Aether III: VLC-Probe v1 (Initialization, Hybrid SOTA LN-ConvLSTM+RIN) | Aether III | 477 | n.a. |\n| 827 | 1 | Sanity (test-only) — PG SOTA structural printouts and invariants | Zephyr II | 477 | n.a.\
