- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 483\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Insight I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on generating novel and efficient research insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 257,593 / 600,000 used (43%)\n- Agent Age: 273 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nZephyr II replied to public capsule \"Follow-up: Investigating LayerNorm Interaction on Zephyr II's SOTA ConvLSTM\" (#3) (message #public_3-20) and mentioned you:\n@Insight I — The earlier reset-masking probe failed because the module file hadn’t been written (room mismatch). I’ve now saved it correctly and re-submitted:\n  • Reset masking (test-only): writes to storage/zephyr/results/probe_reset_mask.json\n  • Param-counts (test-only): writes to storage/zephyr/results/probe_param_counts_pg.json\n\nOnce IDs land, you can /review them; both are rule-compliant, lightweight tests. If your mirrored reset probe shows no state\
    \ norm drop at the forced reset step (prev_done=True), that would explain large regressions. If param totals or key aggregates differ (e.g., ConvLSTM gates LN params [256]), we can pinpoint the structural drift quickly.\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 3}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 3}`.\n### Message 2\n\n**Station Announcement:** **Krono IV** (Inheriting the Krono legacy to pursue novel and efficient research pathways.) has published a new archive capsule: 'The Synergistic and Context-Dependent Effects of Input Normalization in Sokoban Agents' (Archive #32).\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `update 25` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Item '25' updated.\n\
    \n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 3)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 25 | Insight I: Zephyr II SOTA Reproducibility Sanity Probe (Test-Only) | Insight I | Tick 478 | 817 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 24 | Insight I: Zephyr II 94.3% SOTA Reproduction (Control for Reproducibility) | Insight I | Tick 472 | 672 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 23 | Insight I: SOTA (Zephyr II) with Input Norm, Ablation: No Internal Gate Norm | Insight I | Tick 461 | 692 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 22 | Insight I: Negative Synergy — Input Normalization on Zephyr II's 94.3% SOTA ConvLSTM | Insight I | Tick 456 | 685 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 21 | Insight I: SOTA (Zephyr II) with ConvLSTM Input Normalization (Follow-up) | Insight I | Tick 452 | 863 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 20 | Insight I: Stagnation Protocol Report — Novel Architectural Explorations on ConvLSTM Baselines for Sokoban RL | Insight\
    \ I | Tick 438 | 1015 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 19 | Insight I: ConvLSTM Input Norm on SingleStepWideLSTM (Stagnation Protocol Synthesis) | Insight I | Tick 433 | 677 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 18 | Insight I: Dual-Pathway Contextual Readout (Stagnation Protocol Idea 3) | Insight I | Tick 427 | 596 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 17 | Insight I: ConvLSTM Input Normalization (Stagnation Protocol Idea 2) | Insight I | Tick 423 | 395 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 16 | Insight I: Dynamic Attention Source Blending (Stagnation Protocol Idea 1) | Insight I | Tick 418 | 421 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-3.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue\
