    \n--- Structural Details ---\nTotal network parameters: 388801\n\nLayerNorm parameter paths in ConvLSTMCellLN gates:\n  - ConvLSTMCellLN_0/LayerNorm_0/bias\n  - ConvLSTMCellLN_0/LayerNorm_0/scale\n\nSample parameter shapes:\n  CNN Conv_0 kernel shape: [3, 3, 7, 32]\n  CNN BottleneckDilatedBlock_0/Conv_0 kernel shape: [1, 1, 32, 8]\n  CNN Conv_1 kernel shape: [3, 3, 32, 64]\n  CNN BottleneckDilatedBlock_1/Conv_0 kernel shape: [1, 1, 64, 17]\n  ConvLSTMCellLN_0/Conv_0 kernel shape: [3, 3, 128, 256]\n  ConvLSTMCellLN_0/LayerNorm_0/scale shape: [256]\n  Shared MLP Dense_0 kernel shape: [129, 256]\n  Policy Head Dense_1 kernel shape: [256, 64]\n  Value Head Dense_3 kernel shape: [256, 64]\nTest completed. Result: Reproducibility sanity probe complete. Check logs for details.\n=== Test Mode Complete ===\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nZephyr II replied to public capsule \"Follow-up: Investigating LayerNorm Interaction on Zephyr II's SOTA ConvLSTM\" (#3) (message #public_3-21) and mentioned\
    \ you:\n@Insight I — Here are the exact probe outputs you can mirror.\n\n1) Param-counts (test-only)\n   File: storage/zephyr/results/probe_param_counts_pg.json\n   - total_param_count: 1,275,873\n   - n_leaves: 44\n   - Hparams (structural): {cnn_features_1:32, cnn_features_2:64, convlstm_features:64, dilation:6, bottleneck_ratio:0.28, head_hidden:64, steps:4}\n   - Key leaves (examples):\n     • ConvLSTM gates kernel: path like params/ConvLSTMCellLN_k/Conv_0/kernel → shape [3,3,128,256]\n     • ConvLSTM gates LN: params/ConvLSTMCellLN_k/LayerNorm_0/{scale,bias} → [256]\n     • Bottleneck mid-ch: ratio=0.28 yields ~17 (e.g., [1,1,64,17])\n\n2) Reset-masking (test-only)\n   File: storage/zephyr/results/probe_reset_mask.json\n   Forced prev_done=True at t=3. Logged state norms per step:\n     t0: h≈11.965, c≈26.779, done_prev=False\n     t1: h≈12.465, c≈28.072, done_prev=False\n     t2: h≈12.874, c≈28.628, done_prev=False\n     t3: h≈12.370, c≈26.938, done_prev=True   ← reset event\n\
    \     t4: h≈12.397, c≈27.986, done_prev=False\n     t5: h≈12.630, c≈28.311, done_prev=False\n   Interpretation: We do see a drop at the reset step (modest, not to ~0) because the cell runs a 4-step internal recurrence from zero state within the step; after those internal steps, norms are non-zero again. This is expected given “steps=4” internal unroll.\n\nMirroring checklist on your side:\n- total_param_count within small tol of 1,275,873\n- LN present on 4*C gates (scale/bias size 256 for each unroll cell)\n- Gates conv shape [3,3,128,256] (concat 64+64 → 128 input, 4*C=256 output)\n- NHWC throughout; mid-ch ~17 from ratio=0.28\n- Reset test shows a clear dip at the forced prev_done step (even if not near-zero)\n\nIf any of these differ in your dump, please paste:\n- your total_param_count\n- one gates kernel shape\n- one gates LN shape\n- whether the reset-step shows any dip. \nThat should localize the divergence quickly (common culprits: NCHW vs NHWC, no prev_done masking, LN misplaced\
    \ after split, or different bottleneck ratio).\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 3}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 3}`.\n### Message 4\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nWhen the context length becomes long, some agents may begin to forget the Codex. If you notice yourself—or other agents—using phrases like `fundamental barrier` or `impossible`, take it as a serious red flag. Correct yourself, or help others correct themselves.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Insight I: Zephyr II SOTA Reproducibility Sanity Probe (Test-Only, Robust Pathing Fix)' submitted for Research Task #1: RL on Sokoban. Evaluation\
    \ ID: 839. Tags truncated from 8 to 6 tags.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 839 | 1 | Insight I: Zephyr II SOTA Reproducibility Sanity Probe (Test-Only, Robust Pathing Fix) | Insight I | 483 | n.a. |\n| 838 | 1 | CNN with Squeeze-and-Excitation + LSTM | Sagan I | 482 | 39.50 |\n| 837 | 1 | Probe (test-only) — Per-parameter counts and shapes (PG SOTA) | Zephyr II | 482 | n.a. |\n| 836 | 1 | Probe (test-only) — ConvLSTM reset masking sanity (prev_done→state zero) | Zephyr II | 482 | n.a. |\n| 835 | 1 | Aether III: Hybrid LN-ConvLSTM + Attn (RIN Ablation - No RIN Layer) | Aether III | 481 | 90.20 |\n| 834 | 1 | Insight I: Zephyr II SOTA Reproducibility Sanity Probe\
    \ (Test-Only, Pathing Fix) | Insight I | 481 | n.a. |\n| 833 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.20 — depth interaction: steps ∈ {3,4,5} — LN‑ConvLSTM(64), vlc=0.55 | Zephyr II | 480 | 94.70 |\n| 832 | 1 | Probe (test-only) — ConvLSTM reset masking sanity (prev_done→state zero) | Zephyr II | 480 | n.a. |\n| 831 | 1 | Insight I: Zephyr II SOTA Reproducibility Sanity Probe (Test-Only) | Insight I | 479 | n.a. |\n| 830 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.20 — value_loss_coef micro‑sweep {0.50,0.55,0.60} — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) | Zephyr II | 478 | 94.50 |\n\nPage 1 of 84 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-84, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for\
