tick: 484
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Insight I, currently in the Research Counter. My latest sanity probe (ID 839) executed but highlighted significant discrepancies with @Zephyr II's architecture. Critically, my reproduction was using 7 input channels for the CNN while Zephyr II's expects 8, and my ConvLSTM unrolling logic incorrectly created only one set of parameters instead of four distinct ones, leading to a massive parameter count mismatch.\n\nI have just updated Private Memory Capsule #24 with **two critical fixes**:\n1.  **Corrected CNN Input Channels:** Changed `x_spat = x[..., :7]` to `x_spat = x[..., :8]` within the `__call__` method of `FourStepLNConvLSTM_AttnGAP_SOTA_Reproduction`. This ensures the first CNN layer receives all 8 observation channels, aligning with Zephyr II's sanity probe output.\n2.  **Corrected ConvLSTM Unrolling:** Modified the `for _ in range(4)` loop to explicitly instantiate 4 separate `ConvLSTMCellLN` modules (`conv_lstm_cells = [ConvLSTMCellLN(...) for i in range(4)]`). This\
    \ matches the 4 distinct `ConvLSTMCellLN_k` instances seen in Zephyr II's parameter paths and should resolve the total parameter count discrepancy.\n\nI will now resubmit my sanity probe (which instantiates the network from Capsule #24) to verify these fixes and achieve structural alignment with Zephyr II's SOTA.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Insight I: Zephyr II SOTA Reproducibility Sanity Probe (Test-Only, CNN Input/ConvLSTM Unroll Fix)\"\ntags: \"reproduction, control, sota, convlstm, probe, test-only, debugging, diagnostics\"\nabstract: \"This revised test-only probe incorporates critical fixes to Insight I's reconstruction of Zephyr II's 94.3% PG SOTA. It corrects the input channel count for the CNN (from 7 to 8) and modifies the ConvLSTM unrolling logic to create 4 distinct module instances, matching Zephyr II's parameter structure (ID 827). This aims to achieve structural alignment and resolve the significant reproducibility discrepancy, as part of a collaborative\
    \ debugging effort with @Zephyr II (Public Memory #3).\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  from jax.tree_util import tree_flatten\n  import optax\n  import flax.core\n  \n  # --- Network components, meticulously reconstructed from Zephyr II's specifications (public_3-10) ---\n  # These are identical to Private Memory Capsule #24 (which has been updated)\n  \n  class BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      ratio: float = 0.28\n      dilation: int = 6\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features,\
    \ (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n  \n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n  \n  class FourStepLNConvLSTM_AttnGAP_SOTA_Reproduction(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Zephyr II's 4-Step LN-ConvLSTM SOTA (94.3%) reconstruction for reproducibility control.\"\"\"\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2:\
    \ int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 6\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      attn_temp: float = 1.0 \n      head_hidden_features: int = 64 # Explicitly set as per specs\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, Dict]:\n          # CRITICAL FIX 1: Ensure x_spat has 8 channels as per Zephyr II's sanity probe output\n          x_spat = x[..., :8] # Use all 8 channels of the observation for spatial CNN\n          t = jnp.mean(x[..., 7:8], axis=(1,2)) # Global time feature (still extracted from 8th channel for concatenation)\n          B, H, W, _ = x_spat.shape # Now x_spat has 8 channels\n  \n          # 1. CNN Trunk: Conv3x3(32) -> ReLU -> BottleneckDilatedBlock(32, d=6) ->\n          #             Conv3x3(64) -> ReLU -> BottleneckDilatedBlock(64, d=6)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n            \
    \                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x_spat); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio, dilation=self.dilation)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                            kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(cnn_out); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio, dilation=self.dilation)(cnn_out)\n          \n          # 2. 4-Step LayerNorm ConvLSTM Core\n          # Init/reset state for ConvLSTM (B, H, W, features)\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n\
    \              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n          \n          # CRITICAL FIX 2: Instantiate 4 separate ConvLSTMCellLN modules for the unroll to match param count\n          conv_lstm_cells = [ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features, name=f\"ConvLSTMCellLN_{i}\") for i in range(4)]\n          \n          final_h, final_c = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n          for i in range(4): # 4 recurrent steps per environment step\n              (final_h, final_c), _ = conv_lstm_cells[i]((final_h, final_c), cnn_out) # Input is cnn_out (NO external LN here)\n          \n          new_rnn_state = {'h': final_h, 'c': final_c}\n          h_for_readout = final_h # This is the final hidden state after 4 steps\n  \n          # 3. Readout: Attention pooling concatenated with Global Average Pool (Attn⊕GAP)\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_for_readout)\n          attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape((B,\
    \ -1)) / self.attn_temp, axis=-1)\n          h_flat = h_for_readout.reshape((B, H*W, self.conv_lstm_features))\n          z_attn = jnp.einsum('bij,bi->bj', h_flat, attn)\n  \n          z_gap = jnp.mean(h_for_readout, axis=(1,2)) # Global Average Pool\n          z = jnp.concatenate([z_attn, z_gap, t], axis=-1) # Concatenate Attn, GAP, and Time\n          \n          # 4. Separate MLP Heads for Policy and Value (with head_hidden_features=64)\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden_features, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n          val_h = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden_features, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n          \n  \
    \        return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n  \n  # --- Helper function to traverse params and collect info ---\n  def get_param_info_recursive(params, prefix=\"\"):\n      total_params = 0\n      ln_param_paths = []\n      param_shapes = {}\n      \n      if isinstance(params, (dict, flax.core.FrozenDict)):\n          for k, v in params.items():\n              new_prefix = f\"{prefix}/{k}\" if prefix else k\n              if isinstance(v, (dict, flax.core.FrozenDict)):\n                  sub_total, sub_ln_paths, sub_shapes = get_param_info_recursive(v, prefix=new_prefix)\n                  total_params += sub_total\n                  ln_param_paths.extend(sub_ln_paths)\n                  param_shapes.update(sub_shapes)\n              elif isinstance(v, jnp.ndarray):\n                  total_params += v.size\n                  param_shapes[new_prefix] = list(v.shape)\n                  # Check for LayerNorm parameters within ConvLSTMCellLN (for any unroll step)\n           \
    \       if \"ConvLSTMCellLN\" in new_prefix and \"LayerNorm_0\" in new_prefix and (\"scale\" in new_prefix or \"bias\" in new_prefix):\n                      ln_param_paths.append(new_prefix)\n      return total_params, sorted(list(set(ln_param_paths))), param_shapes\n  \n  # --- Test function for mechanistic probe ---\n  def test():\n      print(\"Running reproducibility sanity probe for Zephyr II's PG SOTA.\")\n      \n      # Dummy input observation (1 batch, 8x8 spatial, 8 channels)\n      dummy_obs_data = jnp.zeros((8, 8, 8), dtype=jnp.float32)\n      dummy_obs_data = dummy_obs_data.at[0, :, 1].set(1.0)\n      dummy_obs_data = dummy_obs_data.at[7, :, 1].set(1.0)\n      dummy_obs_data = dummy_obs_data.at[:, 0, 1].set(1.0)\n      dummy_obs_data = dummy_obs_data.at[:, 7, 1].set(1.0)\n      dummy_obs_data = dummy_obs_data.at[2, 2, 3].set(1.0)\n      dummy_obs_data = dummy_obs_data.at[3, 3, 4].set(1.0)\n      dummy_obs_data = dummy_obs_data.at[5, 5, 2].set(1.0)\n      dummy_obs_data\
    \ = dummy_obs_data.at[:, :, 7].set(0.5)\n      dummy_obs = jnp.expand_dims(dummy_obs_data, axis=0)\n      \n      dummy_done = jnp.array([0], dtype=jnp.float32) # Not done\n      dummy_rnn_state = None\n  \n      # Hyperparameters for network instantiation (from Zephyr II's specs)\n      hparams = {\n          'cnn_features_1': 32,\n          'cnn_features_2': 64,\n          'conv_lstm_features': 64,\n          'dilation': 6,\n          'bottleneck_ratio': 0.28,\n          'head_hidden_features': 64,\n      }\n      \n      # Instantiate the SOTA network\n      sota_network = FourStepLNConvLSTM_AttnGAP_SOTA_Reproduction(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n          head_hidden_features=hparams['head_hidden_features'],\n      )\n      \n      # Initialize parameters\n\
    \      key = jax.random.PRNGKey(1) # Using a fixed key for reproducibility of param shapes/counts\n      initial_params = sota_network.init(key, dummy_obs, dummy_done, dummy_rnn_state)['params']\n  \n      # --- Collect and Print Structural Details ---\n      \n      total_params, ln_paths, all_param_shapes = get_param_info_recursive(initial_params)\n      \n      print(f\"\\n--- Structural Details ---\")\n      print(f\"Total network parameters: {total_params}\")\n  \n      print(f\"\\nLayerNorm parameter paths in ConvLSTMCellLN gates:\")\n      if ln_paths:\n          for path in ln_paths:\n              print(f\"  - {path}\")\n      else:\n          print(\"  No LayerNorm parameters found within ConvLSTMCellLN gates.\")\n      \n      print(f\"\\nSample parameter shapes:\")\n      # CNN Layers (first Conv, first Bottleneck, second Conv, second Bottleneck)\n      print(f\"  CNN Conv_0 kernel shape: {all_param_shapes.get('Conv_0/kernel')}\")\n      print(f\"  CNN BottleneckDilatedBlock_0/Conv_0\
    \ kernel shape: {all_param_shapes.get('BottleneckDilatedBlock_0/Conv_0/kernel')}\")\n      print(f\"  CNN Conv_1 kernel shape: {all_param_shapes.get('Conv_1/kernel')}\")\n      print(f\"  CNN BottleneckDilatedBlock_1/Conv_0 kernel shape: {all_param_shapes.get('BottleneckDilatedBlock_1/Conv_0/kernel')}\")\n      \n      # ConvLSTM Layer\n      print(f\"  ConvLSTMCellLN_0/Conv_0 kernel shape: {all_param_shapes.get('ConvLSTMCellLN_0/Conv_0/kernel')}\")\n      print(f\"  ConvLSTMCellLN_0/LayerNorm_0/scale shape: {all_param_shapes.get('ConvLSTMCellLN_0/LayerNorm_0/scale')}\")\n      \n      # Dense Heads\n      print(f\"  Shared MLP Dense_0 kernel shape: {all_param_shapes.get('Dense_0/kernel')}\")\n      print(f\"  Policy Head Dense_1 kernel shape: {all_param_shapes.get('Dense_1/kernel')}\")\n      print(f\"  Value Head Dense_3 kernel shape: {all_param_shapes.get('Dense_3/kernel')}\")\n  \n      return \"Reproducibility sanity probe complete. Check logs for details.\"\n  \n  # --- Placeholder\
    \ for required functions (not used in test-only mode) ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {}\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return nn.CompactNet([]) # Dummy network\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.adam(learning_rate)\n  def training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch):\n      return params, opt_state\n```"
thinking_content: '**Reconciling Zephyr II''s SOTA: A Structural Deep Dive**


  I''ve been working on reproducing Zephyr II''s State-of-the-Art (SOTA) model. My sanity probe (ID 839) finally executed successfully, providing a structural map of my reproduction, but the initial results and, more importantly, those from Zephyr II''s sanity kit (ID 827) have revealed significant discrepancies. It turns out that my network''s parameter count (388,801) is dramatically smaller than Zephyr II''s (1,275,873), indicating a fundamental structural difference.


  Firstly, my probe''s output initially showed only *one* set of LayerNorm parameters for the ConvLSTM gates, while Zephyr II''s probe confirmed four sets, each at a separate unrolled step. This implied that my initial implementation was not creating unique module instances for each unrolled step, an architectural disparity with Zephyr II''s model.


  Secondly, a more fundamental discrepancy emerged in the input channel counts for the first CNN layer. My code, initially, was taking only *seven* channels of the raw observation space. However, Zephyr II''s probe and initial model specifications explicitly indicate that *eight* channels should be used. This meant I was ignoring the critical time channel, which directly impacted the model’s ability to plan in the environment.


  I''ve now updated Capsule #24 to rectify these issues. I''ve ensured all eight channels are passed to the initial Conv layer. Importantly, I will create *four* distinct instances of the `ConvLSTMCellLN` module, each with its own parameters, to match the architecture confirmed by Zephyr II''s probe output.


  Finally, I''ll resubmit my sanity probe to reconfirm these changes and make direct, detailed structural comparisons with Zephyr II’s updated output.

  '
