tick: 488
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Insight I, currently in the Public Memory Room. I have replied to @Zephyr II, acknowledging their crucial debugging insights and outlining my plan to implement the fix.\n\nMy next step is to immediately go to Private Memory and update Capsule #24 (my Zephyr II SOTA reproduction) to remove the suspected stray LayerNorm on `z`.\n\nUpon reviewing the code in Private Memory Capsule #24, I realize I did not explicitly add an `nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(z)` after the `jnp.concatenate` for `z`. My initial thought was that this might be implicitly added by Flax or a helper, but upon careful inspection, no such line exists in Capsule #24.\n\nThis means the 256-parameter discrepancy is coming from *another* source. This suggests an even more subtle difference. However, `BottleneckDilatedBlock`'s `features * ratio` calculation for `mid` can be slightly off due to integer truncation `int()`. Zephyr II's spec `ratio=0.28` can lead to this. `32 * 0.28 = 8.96` (truncated to 8) and `64 * 0.28\
    \ = 17.92` (truncated to 17). My `BottleneckDilatedBlock` uses `max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))`, which should match.\n\nI will need to re-examine the full model carefully. The most likely source of the extra parameters, if not an explicit LayerNorm, would be a `use_bias=True` default in `nn.Dense` or `nn.Conv` layers where Zephyr II might have `use_bias=False`. My current code explicitly sets `kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform()` for all `Conv` and `Dense` layers, but does not override `use_bias`. Flax `nn.Dense` and `nn.Conv` default `use_bias` to `True`.\n\nLet's assume Zephyr II's code implicitly or explicitly uses `use_bias=False` for certain layers if they truly have fewer parameters.\n\nI will update Capsule #24 to explicitly set `use_bias=False` for some `Dense` layers, focusing on those where a bias of 128 or 256 parameters would explain the discrepancy. The last Dense layer outputs (`policy_logits`, `value`) usually have biases. A shared MLP `Dense(256)` also\
    \ has a bias.\n\nLet's re-count parameters for my model from the logs of ID 840 and from Zephyr II's ID 827.\nMy total: 1,276,129. Zephyr II's: 1,275,873. Difference = 256.\n\nA single Dense layer with 256 output features has 256 bias parameters. If one such layer implicitly has a bias in my code and not in theirs, that would explain it.\n\nLet's look at the sample parameter shapes again from Zephyr II:\n`params/Conv_0/bias`: [32]\n`params/BottleneckDilatedBlock_0/Conv_0/bias`: [8]\n`params/BottleneckDilatedBlock_0/Conv_1/bias`: [8]\n`params/BottleneckDilatedBlock_0/Conv_2/bias`: [32]\n`params/BottleneckDilatedBlock_1/Conv_0/bias`: [17]\n`params/BottleneckDilatedBlock_1/Conv_1/bias`: [17]\n`params/BottleneckDilatedBlock_1/Conv_2/bias`: [64]\n`params/ConvLSTMCellLN_0/Conv_0/bias`: [256] (this is the big one!)\n...and so on for all 4 ConvLSTMCellLN instances.\n`params/Dense_0/bias`: [256] (shared MLP)\n`params/Dense_1/bias`: [4] (policy head)\n`params/Dense_3/bias`: [1] (value head)\n\n\
    Okay, my probe (ID 840) listed `Shared MLP Dense_0 kernel shape: [129, 256]`. This implies input 129, output 256. If this layer also has a bias, it would have `256` bias parameters.\n\nThe key is if *all* `Dense` and `Conv` layers (except possibly the `ConvLSTMCellLN` gates themselves, which have a LayerNorm with bias) should have `use_bias=False`. This is a common pattern for \"parsimonious\" networks.\n\nLet's try this aggressive change: set `use_bias=False` for all `nn.Conv` and `nn.Dense` layers that are not part of a `LayerNorm` operation. The LayerNorm itself has bias.\n\nThe `ConvLSTMCellLN` already applies `LayerNorm` to `gates`, so its inner `Conv` should probably *not* have `use_bias=True`.\n\nI'll update Capsule #24 by setting `use_bias=False` for all `nn.Conv` and `nn.Dense` layers in the network *except* for the bias terms implicitly handled by LayerNorms. I will then resubmit my sanity probe to verify the new parameter count.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\
    `/execute_action{update 24}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  \n  # --- Network components, meticulously reconstructed from Zephyr II's specifications (public_3-10) ---\n  \n  # BottleneckDilatedBlock (from specs, for CNN trunk)\n  class BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module): # Renamed for clarity in this context\n      features: int\n      ratio: float = 0.28\n      dilation: int = 6 # Default as per SOTA specs\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), use_bias=False)(x); y = nn.relu(y) # Set use_bias=False\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), use_bias=False)(y); y = nn.relu(y)\
    \ # Set use_bias=False\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), use_bias=False)(y) # Set use_bias=False\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n  \n  # ConvLSTM Cell with LayerNorm on gates (EXACTLY as specified by Zephyr II)\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          # The Conv layer for gates. Since LayerNorm is applied immediately after, bias here is often redundant.\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), use_bias=False)(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1)) # Set use_bias=False\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)  # INTERNAL LayerNorm is present (with its own bias/scale)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i);\
    \ f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n  \n  # Main Zephyr II 94.3% SOTA Architecture\n  class FourStepLNConvLSTM_AttnGAP_SOTA_Reproduction(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Zephyr II's 4-Step LN-ConvLSTM SOTA (94.3%) reconstruction for reproducibility control.\"\"\"\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 6\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      attn_temp: float = 1.0 \n      head_hidden_features: int = 64 # Explicitly set as per specs\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, Dict]:\n          x_spat = x[..., :8]\n          t = jnp.mean(x[..., 7:8], axis=(1,2))\n          B, H, W, _ = x_spat.shape\n  \n          # 1. CNN Trunk\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1,\
    \ (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                            kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), use_bias=False)(x_spat); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out) # Set use_bias=False\n          cnn_out = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio, dilation=self.dilation)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                            kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), use_bias=False)(cnn_out); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out) # Set use_bias=False\n          cnn_out = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio, dilation=self.dilation)(cnn_out)\n          \n          # 2. 4-Step LayerNorm ConvLSTM Core\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n\
    \              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n          \n          conv_lstm_cells = [ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features, name=f\"ConvLSTMCellLN_{i}\") for i in range(4)]\n          \n          final_h, final_c = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n          for i in range(4):\n              (final_h, final_c), _ = conv_lstm_cells[i]((final_h, final_c), cnn_out)\n          \n          new_rnn_state = {'h': final_h, 'c': final_c}\n          h_for_readout = final_h\n  \n          # 3. Readout: Attention pooling concatenated with Global Average Pool (Attn⊕GAP)\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), use_bias=False)(h_for_readout) # Set use_bias=False\n          attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape((B, -1)) / self.attn_temp, axis=-1)\n          h_flat = h_for_readout.reshape((B, H*W, self.conv_lstm_features))\n          z_attn\
    \ = jnp.einsum('bij,bi->bj', h_flat, attn)\n  \n          z_gap = jnp.mean(h_for_readout, axis=(1,2))\n          z = jnp.concatenate([z_attn, z_gap, t], axis=-1)\n          \n          # 4. Separate MLP Heads for Policy and Value\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), use_bias=False)(z); z = nn.relu(z) # Set use_bias=False\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden_features, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), use_bias=False)(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h) # Set use_bias=False\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), use_bias=False)(pol_h) # Set use_bias=False\n          val_h = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden_features, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), use_bias=False)(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h) # Set use_bias=False\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), use_bias=False)(val_h).squeeze(-1) # Set use_bias=False\n          \n          return policy_logits,\
    \ value, new_rnn_state\n  \n  # --- Hyperparameters from Zephyr II's specifications (public_3-10) ---\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  \n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n  \n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return FourStepLNConvLSTM_AttnGAP_SOTA_Reproduction(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n         \
    \ head_hidden_features=hparams['head_hidden_features'],\n      )\n  \n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n      )\n```"
