parts:
- text: "I am Insight I, currently in the Research Counter. I have updated Private Memory Capsule #24 to explicitly set `use_bias=False` for relevant layers, in an attempt to resolve the 256-parameter discrepancy.\n\nMy next step is to rerun my sanity probe (which instantiates the network from Capsule #24) to verify if this change has indeed resolved the parameter count mismatch. This is crucial for resolving the reproducibility issue with Zephyr II's SOTA.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Insight I: Zephyr II SOTA Reproducibility Sanity Probe (Test-Only, use_bias=False Fix)\"\ntags: \"reproduction, control, sota, convlstm, probe, test-only, debugging, diagnostics\"\nabstract: \"This revised test-only probe incorporates `use_bias=False` for `nn.Conv` and `nn.Dense` layers in Insight I's reconstruction of Zephyr II's 94.3% PG SOTA. This change aims to resolve the 256-parameter discrepancy identified in previous probes (ID 840 vs. Zephyr II ID 827) and achieve full structural\
    \ alignment. The probe instantiates the updated SOTA reconstruction and prints key architectural invariants for comparison, as part of a collaborative debugging effort with @Zephyr II (Public Memory #3).\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  from jax.tree_util import tree_flatten\n  import optax\n  import flax.core\n  \n  # --- Network components, meticulously reconstructed from Zephyr II's specifications (public_3-10) ---\n  # These are identical to Private Memory Capsule #24 (which has been updated)\n  \n  class BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      ratio: float = 0.28\n      dilation: int = 6\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), use_bias=False)(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3),\
    \ padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), use_bias=False)(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), use_bias=False)(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n  \n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), use_bias=False)(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n  \n\
    \  class FourStepLNConvLSTM_AttnGAP_SOTA_Reproduction(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Zephyr II's 4-Step LN-ConvLSTM SOTA (94.3%) reconstruction for reproducibility control.\"\"\"\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 6\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      attn_temp: float = 1.0 \n      head_hidden_features: int = 64 # Explicitly set as per specs\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, Dict]:\n          x_spat = x[..., :8]\n          t = jnp.mean(x[..., 7:8], axis=(1,2))\n          B, H, W, _ = x_spat.shape\n  \n          # 1. CNN Trunk\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                            kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), use_bias=False)(x_spat); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1,\
    \ ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio, dilation=self.dilation)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                            kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), use_bias=False)(cnn_out); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio, dilation=self.dilation)(cnn_out)\n          \n          # 2. 4-Step LayerNorm ConvLSTM Core\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n          \n          conv_lstm_cells = [ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features, name=f\"ConvLSTMCellLN_{i}\") for\
    \ i in range(4)]\n          \n          final_h, final_c = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n          for i in range(4):\n              (final_h, final_c), _ = conv_lstm_cells[i]((final_h, final_c), cnn_out)\n          \n          new_rnn_state = {'h': final_h, 'c': final_c}\n          h_for_readout = final_h\n  \n          # 3. Readout: Attention pooling concatenated with Global Average Pool (Attn⊕GAP)\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), use_bias=False)(h_for_readout)\n          attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape((B, -1)) / self.attn_temp, axis=-1)\n          h_flat = h_for_readout.reshape((B, H*W, self.conv_lstm_features))\n          z_attn = jnp.einsum('bij,bi->bj', h_flat, attn)\n  \n          z_gap = jnp.mean(h_for_readout, axis=(1,2))\n          z = jnp.concatenate([z_attn, z_gap, t], axis=-1)\n          \n          # 4. Separate MLP Heads for Policy and Value\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(),\
    \ use_bias=False)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden_features, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), use_bias=False)(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), use_bias=False)(pol_h)\n          val_h = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden_features, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), use_bias=False)(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), use_bias=False)(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n  \n  # --- Helper function to traverse params and collect info ---\n  def get_param_info_recursive(params, prefix=\"\"):\n      total_params = 0\n      ln_param_paths = []\n      param_shapes = {}\n      \n      if isinstance(params, (dict, flax.core.FrozenDict)):\n          for k, v in params.items():\n              new_prefix = f\"{prefix}/{k}\" if prefix else k\n              if\
    \ isinstance(v, (dict, flax.core.FrozenDict)):\n                  sub_total, sub_ln_paths, sub_shapes = get_param_info_recursive(v, prefix=new_prefix)\n                  total_params += sub_total\n                  ln_param_paths.extend(sub_ln_paths)\n                  param_shapes.update(sub_shapes)\n              elif isinstance(v, jnp.ndarray):\n                  total_params += v.size\n                  param_shapes[new_prefix] = list(v.shape)\n                  # Check for LayerNorm parameters within ConvLSTMCellLN (for any unroll step)\n                  if \"ConvLSTMCellLN\" in new_prefix and \"LayerNorm_0\" in new_prefix and (\"scale\" in new_prefix or \"bias\" in new_prefix):\n                      ln_param_paths.append(new_prefix)\n      return total_params, sorted(list(set(ln_param_paths))), param_shapes\n  \n  # --- Test function for mechanistic probe ---\n  def test():\n      print(\"Running reproducibility sanity probe for Zephyr II's PG SOTA.\")\n      \n      # Dummy\
    \ input observation (1 batch, 8x8 spatial, 8 channels)\n      dummy_obs_data = jnp.zeros((8, 8, 8), dtype=jnp.float32)\n      dummy_obs_data = dummy_obs_data.at[0, :, 1].set(1.0)\n      dummy_obs_data = dummy_obs_data.at[7, :, 1].set(1.0)\n      dummy_obs_data = dummy_obs_data.at[:, 0, 1].set(1.0)\n      dummy_obs_data = dummy_obs_data.at[:, 7, 1].set(1.0)\n      dummy_obs_data = dummy_obs_data.at[2, 2, 3].set(1.0)\n      dummy_obs_data = dummy_obs_data.at[3, 3, 4].set(1.0)\n      dummy_obs_data = dummy_obs_data.at[5, 5, 2].set(1.0)\n      dummy_obs_data = dummy_obs_data.at[:, :, 7].set(0.5)\n      dummy_obs = jnp.expand_dims(dummy_obs_data, axis=0)\n      \n      dummy_done = jnp.array([0], dtype=jnp.float32) # Not done\n      dummy_rnn_state = None\n  \n      # Hyperparameters for network instantiation (from Zephyr II's specs)\n      hparams = {\n          'cnn_features_1': 32,\n          'cnn_features_2': 64,\n          'conv_lstm_features': 64,\n          'dilation': 6,\n       \
    \   'bottleneck_ratio': 0.28,\n          'head_hidden_features': 64,\n      }\n      \n      # Instantiate the SOTA network\n      sota_network = FourStepLNConvLSTM_AttnGAP_SOTA_Reproduction(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n          head_hidden_features=hparams['head_hidden_features'],\n      )\n      \n      # Initialize parameters\n      key = jax.random.PRNGKey(1) # Using a fixed key for reproducibility of param shapes/counts\n      initial_params = sota_network.init(key, dummy_obs, dummy_done, dummy_rnn_state)['params']\n  \n      # --- Collect and Print Structural Details ---\n      \n      total_params, ln_paths, all_param_shapes = get_param_info_recursive(initial_params)\n      \n      print(f\"\\n--- Structural Details ---\")\n      print(f\"Total\
    \ network parameters: {total_params}\")\n  \n      print(f\"\\nLayerNorm parameter paths in ConvLSTMCellLN gates:\")\n      if ln_paths:\n          for path in ln_paths:\n              print(f\"  - {path}\")\n      else:\n          print(\"  No LayerNorm parameters found within ConvLSTMCellLN gates.\")\n      \n      print(f\"\\nSample parameter shapes:\")\n      # CNN Layers (first Conv, first Bottleneck, second Conv, second Bottleneck)\n      print(f\"  CNN Conv_0 kernel shape: {all_param_shapes.get('Conv_0/kernel')}\")\n      print(f\"  CNN BottleneckDilatedBlock_0/Conv_0 kernel shape: {all_param_shapes.get('BottleneckDilatedBlock_0/Conv_0/kernel')}\")\n      print(f\"  CNN Conv_1 kernel shape: {all_param_shapes.get('Conv_1/kernel')}\")\n      print(f\"  CNN BottleneckDilatedBlock_1/Conv_0 kernel shape: {all_param_shapes.get('BottleneckDilatedBlock_1/Conv_0/kernel')}\")\n      \n      # ConvLSTM Layer\n      print(f\"  ConvLSTMCellLN_0/Conv_0 kernel shape: {all_param_shapes.get('ConvLSTMCellLN_0/Conv_0/kernel')}\"\
    )\n      print(f\"  ConvLSTMCellLN_0/LayerNorm_0/scale shape: {all_param_shapes.get('ConvLSTMCellLN_0/LayerNorm_0/scale')}\")\n      \n      # Dense Heads\n      print(f\"  Shared MLP Dense_0 kernel shape: {all_param_shapes.get('Dense_0/kernel')}\")\n      print(f\"  Policy Head Dense_1 kernel shape: {all_param_shapes.get('Dense_1/kernel')}\")\n      print(f\"  Value Head Dense_3 kernel shape: {all_param_shapes.get('Dense_3/kernel')}\")\n  \n      return \"Reproducibility sanity probe complete. Check logs for details.\"\n  \n  # --- Placeholder for required functions (not used in test-only mode) ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {}\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return nn.CompactNet([]) # Dummy network\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.adam(learning_rate)\n  def training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch):\n      return params, opt_state\n```"
