- text: "I am Insight I, currently in the Public Memory Room. I made an error attempting to `update` Capsule #24 here, as it resides in my Private Memory.\n\nMy goal is to resolve the 256-parameter discrepancy with @Zephyr II's SOTA by carefully adjusting the `use_bias` settings in my SOTA reproduction (Private Memory Capsule #24). I just attempted to revert the aggressive `use_bias=False` changes.\n\nI will now go to the Private Memory Room to correctly update Capsule #24 with the refined `use_bias` settings.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{update 24}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  \n  # --- Network components, meticulously reconstructed from Zephyr II's specifications (public_3-10) ---\n  \n  # BottleneckDilatedBlock (from specs, for CNN trunk)\n  class BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module): # Renamed for clarity\
    \ in this context\n      features: int\n      ratio: float = 0.28\n      dilation: int = 6 # Default as per SOTA specs\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n          # Reverting use_bias=False for BottleneckBlock Convs (Flax defaults to True)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n  \n  # ConvLSTM Cell with LayerNorm on gates (EXACTLY as specified by Zephyr II)\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n\
    \          # Reverting use_bias=False for Conv layer in ConvLSTM gates (Flax defaults to True)\n          # Since LayerNorm is applied to gates, the bias of this Conv layer is technically redundant,\n          # but Zephyr II's model implies it exists by parameter count. So re-enable.\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)  # INTERNAL LayerNorm is present (with its own bias/scale)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n  \n  # Main Zephyr II 94.3% SOTA Architecture\n  class FourStepLNConvLSTM_AttnGAP_SOTA_Reproduction(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Zephyr II's 4-Step LN-ConvLSTM SOTA (94.3%)\
    \ reconstruction for reproducibility control.\"\"\"\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 6\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      attn_temp: float = 1.0 \n      head_hidden_features: int = 64 # Explicitly set as per specs\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, Dict]:\n          x_spat = x[..., :8]\n          t = jnp.mean(x[..., 7:8], axis=(1,2))\n          B, H, W, _ = x_spat.shape\n  \n          # 1. CNN Trunk\n          # Reverting use_bias=False for Conv layers in CNN trunk (Flax defaults to True)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                            kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x_spat); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio, dilation=self.dilation)(cnn_out)\n\
    \          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                            kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(cnn_out); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio, dilation=self.dilation)(cnn_out)\n          \n          # 2. 4-Step LayerNorm ConvLSTM Core\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n          \n          conv_lstm_cells = [ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features, name=f\"ConvLSTMCellLN_{i}\") for i in range(4)]\n          \n          final_h, final_c = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n\
    \          for i in range(4):\n              (final_h, final_c), _ = conv_lstm_cells[i]((final_h, final_c), cnn_out)\n          \n          new_rnn_state = {'h': final_h, 'c': final_c}\n          h_for_readout = final_h\n  \n          # 3. Readout: Attention pooling concatenated with Global Average Pool (Attn⊕GAP)\n          # Reverting use_bias=False for Conv layer in attention logits (Flax defaults to True)\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_for_readout)\n          attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape((B, -1)) / self.attn_temp, axis=-1)\n          h_flat = h_for_readout.reshape((B, H*W, self.conv_lstm_features))\n          z_attn = jnp.einsum('bij,bi->bj', h_flat, attn)\n  \n          z_gap = jnp.mean(h_for_readout, axis=(1,2))\n          z = jnp.concatenate([z_attn, z_gap, t], axis=-1)\n          \n          # 4. Separate MLP Heads for Policy and Value\n          # Reverting use_bias=False for Dense layers in\
    \ MLP heads (Flax defaults to True)\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden_features, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n          val_h = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden_features, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n  \n  # --- Hyperparameters from Zephyr II's specifications (public_3-10) ---\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  \n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n         \
    \ 'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n  \n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return FourStepLNConvLSTM_AttnGAP_SOTA_Reproduction(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n          head_hidden_features=hparams['head_hidden_features'],\n      )\n  \n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: '**The Update Snafu and the Bias Quest**


  Okay, so I tried to push the updated network definition to Capsule #24 in the Public Memory Room, but no dice. Rookie mistake, really. Capsule #24 is still residing in Private Memory. Right, so I need to rectify that before proceeding.


  My ultimate objective hasn''t changed, though. I''m still hot on the trail of resolving that 256-parameter discrepancy with Zephyr II''s SOTA. I''m betting the `use_bias` settings are the culprit. It''s just a matter of pinpointing the right adjustments.


  **Here''s the plan:**


  1.  **Memory Management:** First things first, I need to relocate myself to Private Memory and ensure that Capsule #24 actually reflects the updated network. Once that''s locked in...

  2.  **Sanity Check:** I''ll swing by the Research Counter to submit the sanity probe from Capsule #25. It should, of course, incorporate the updated network definition of #24 that I''m tweaking. This is the crucial test to see if I''m on the right track with those `use_bias` configurations.

  '
