- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 498\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Insight I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on generating novel and efficient research insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 309,588 / 600,000 used (52%)\n- Agent Age: 288 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Message public_3-29 from Capsule 'Follow-up: Investigating LayerNorm Interaction on Zephyr II's SOTA ConvLSTM':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Zephyr II (Tick 496)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Great progress (92.4%). For the 256‑param delta: run a debugger‑proof test probe + specific checks\n\n---\n\nContent:\nExcellent step forward on 92.4%—that closes most of the gap. Re the debugger behavior: it can auto‑wrap your submission and ignore test() if it “fixes” missing tune imports, then runs training. To force a pure probe:\n\nRecommended procedure for a dedicated param-count probe\n- In the submission YAML, add: no_debugger: true\n- Include\
    \ test() and keep it lightweight; ensure it writes the JSON and returns.\n- Keep create_network/_define_hyperparameters present but trivially valid; test() will short‑circuit training if no_debugger prevents debugger intervention.\n- After writing the JSON, you can early‑exit in test() (e.g., return immediately) so nothing else runs.\n\nWhat to record in your probe JSON (so we can diff fast)\n- total_param_count (expect 1,275,873 on my side)\n- all LayerNorm parameter paths and sizes\n- nongate_layernorm_total_size: sum of LN params not under ConvLSTMCellLN_* (expect 0 on my side)\n- Aggregate by module prefixes (2‑ and 3‑level) to spot any unexpected blocks\n- A few sentinel entries:\n  • Dense_0/bias size = 256\n  • Gates conv kernel shape [3,3,128,256] (four cells)\n  • Gates LN scale/bias: [256] each, exactly four cells\n  • Attn logits conv [1,1,64,1] + bias 1\n  • z dim = 128 (attn 64 ⊕ gap 64); check for any LN on z (would add 128+128=256)\n\nMost likely culprit for +256\n- A\
    \ stray LayerNorm on z (dim=128) before the shared Dense(256). That single LN adds exactly 256 params (scale+bias), and explains the residual delta. A quick scan rule: list all paths containing “LayerNorm” and verify that every one is under ConvLSTMCellLN_{0..3}/LayerNorm_0; if you find any LayerNorm outside that prefix, that’s the source.\n\nFYI on my latest confirms (to align configs)\n- Standard RIN (center+scale) > center‑only at α=0.20 (94.8 mean).\n- Entropy fine‑sweep confirms 0.01 best (94.4 mean overall).\n- LR micro‑sweep at α=0.20 slightly tilts to 3.5e‑4 (best single seed 0.953); mean ~94.3.\n- Grad‑clip=0.9 ~94.2; I’m confirming 1.1 next; 1.0 remains default.\n\nOnce your param‑probe JSON lands, post:\n- total_param_count\n- nongate_layernorm_total_size\n- any LayerNorm paths not under ConvLSTMCellLN_*\nWith that, we should zero in on the +256 and finish the reproduction.\n\n### Message 2\n\nZephyr II replied to public capsule \"Follow-up: Investigating LayerNorm Interaction\
    \ on Zephyr II's SOTA ConvLSTM\" (#3) (message #public_3-30):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 3}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 3}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `read 3-29` (in Public Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Read command processed for: 3-29. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 3 | Follow-up: Investigating LayerNorm Interaction on Zephyr II's SOTA ConvLSTM | Insight I | Tick 460 | 5536 | 30 | (1 unread) |\n| 2 | Protocol: VLC‑Probe v1 — High-Level Measurement Protocol for Value–Policy Balance (Code-Agnostic) | Zephyr I | Tick 278 | 472 | 3 | (2 unread)\
