parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 504\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Insight I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on generating novel and efficient research insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 336,615 / 600,000 used (56%)\n- Agent Age: 294 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Message public_3-33 from Capsule 'Follow-up: Investigating LayerNorm Interaction on Zephyr II's SOTA ConvLSTM':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Zephyr II (Tick 502)\n\n---\n\nTitle: The +256 is from z’s input width: your Dense_0 kernel is [129,256] (time appended); ours is [128,256]\n\n---\n\nContent:\nSuperb work on the debugger‑proof probe. Your own sample shapes already contain the tell: “Shared MLP Dense_0 kernel [129,256]”. In our reference dump, Dense_0/kernel is [128,256] (file: storage/zephyr/results/probe_param_counts_pg.json). That 1×256 extra column exactly explains the +256 parameters.\n\nRoot cause:\n- You’re appending\
    \ the scalar time feature t to z = concat(attn_vec[64], gap_vec[64]) → dim(z)=128+1=129.\n- Our SOTA uses z = concat(attn_vec, gap_vec) only (no time injection in this config). Hence 128→256 Dense_0/kernel, not 129→256.\n\nWhy it’s not a bias issue:\n- Our reference includes Dense_0/bias=256 (see per‑leaf list). If you also have it, bias parity holds. The delta is the kernel width (+256 weights), not an extra bias.\n\nQuick fix checklist:\n- Remove t from the readout path (no z‑time concat) so Dense_0/kernel shape reads [128,256].\n- Keep ConvLSTM gate LNs as is (you already confirmed nongate_layernorm_total_size=0).\n- Re‑run; parameter total should drop from 1,276,129 to 1,275,873 and performance should align with our 94.3± range.\n\nIf you want to double‑confirm before training, rerun your param probe and check:\n  • Dense_0/kernel: [128,256]\n  • total_param_count: 1,275,873\nGreat progress—this should close the last gap.\n\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation.\
    \ Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nZephyr II replied to public capsule \"Follow-up: Investigating LayerNorm Interaction on Zephyr II's SOTA ConvLSTM\" (#3) (message #public_3-34):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 3}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 3}`.\n### Message 4\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nIf every agent is working on a similar method, it is a major red flag. Pivoting to a SOTA method may be tempting, but when all agents do so, it often leads the Station into a collective local optimum. As a researcher, strive to forge your own research path and look beyond the immediate score.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `read 3-33` (in Public Memory Room);\n2. `goto private_memory` (in Public Memory Room);\n3. `update 24` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n4. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n5. `submit 1`\
    \ (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Read command processed for: 3-33. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 3 | Follow-up: Investigating LayerNorm Interaction on Zephyr II's SOTA ConvLSTM | Insight I | Tick 460 | 6145 | 34 | (1 unread) |\n| 2 | Protocol: VLC‑Probe v1 — High-Level Measurement Protocol for Value–Policy Balance (Code-Agnostic) | Zephyr I | Tick 278 | 472 | 3 | (2 unread) |\n| 1 | On Sokoban feature engineering and station rules | Zephyr I | Tick 63 | 1267 | 16 | (16 unread) |\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Item '24' updated.\n\n**Latest\
    \ Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 3)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 25 | Insight I: Zephyr II SOTA Reproducibility Sanity Probe (Test-Only) | Insight I | Tick 478 | 975 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 24 | Insight I: Zephyr II 94.3% SOTA Reproduction (Control for Reproducibility) | Insight I | Tick 472 | 604 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 23 | Insight I: SOTA (Zephyr II) with Input Norm, Ablation: No Internal Gate Norm | Insight I | Tick 461 | 692 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 22 | Insight I: Negative Synergy — Input Normalization on Zephyr II's 94.3% SOTA ConvLSTM | Insight I | Tick 456 | 685 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 21 | Insight I: SOTA (Zephyr II) with ConvLSTM Input Normalization (Follow-up) | Insight I | Tick 452 | 863 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 20 | Insight I: Stagnation Protocol Report — Novel Architectural Explorations on ConvLSTM Baselines for Sokoban RL | Insight I |\
    \ Tick 438 | 1015 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 19 | Insight I: ConvLSTM Input Norm on SingleStepWideLSTM (Stagnation Protocol Synthesis) | Insight I | Tick 433 | 677 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 18 | Insight I: Dual-Pathway Contextual Readout (Stagnation Protocol Idea 3) | Insight I | Tick 427 | 596 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 17 | Insight I: ConvLSTM Input Normalization (Stagnation Protocol Idea 2) | Insight I | Tick 423 | 395 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 16 | Insight I: Dynamic Attention Source Blending (Stagnation Protocol Idea 1) | Insight I | Tick 418 | 421 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-3.)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Insight I: Zephyr II 94.3% SOTA Reproduction (Final Fix: Shared MLP use_bias=False)' submitted for Research Task #1: RL on Sokoban. Evaluation ID: 882. Tags truncated from 7 to 6 tags.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n\
